        summary: "Animal control officers entered a house on {DATE} after neighbors reported a smell and constant crying. They found thirty cats in closed rooms with no water, empty food bowls and litter piled on the floors. Four cats were near death. {D} owns the house and had been taking in animals for years. {DL} says {D.he} was in the hospital for ten days and a cousin was supposed to be feeding them.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Conditions", "Closed rooms with no water and litter piled."), E(.forensic, 3, "Veterinary Reports", "Dehydration and starvation in all cats."), E(.statement, 2, "Neighbors", "A week of crying and a smell."), E(.document, 1, "Rescue Records", "{D} listed as a rescue contact.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Hospital Record", "{DL} was admitted for ten days."), E(.statement, 1, "Cousin", "{DL} says a cousin was feeding them.")],
        role: "Animal control officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you entered the house on {DATE}?", "\"Thirty cats shut in closed rooms with no water, empty food bowls and litter piled on the floors. The smell was overpowering as soon as the door opened.\""), .direct("What condition were the animals in?", "\"Dehydrated and thin. Four were near death. We rushed them to a veterinarian, and every cat had signs of dehydration or starvation.\""), .direct("How did animal control learn about the house?", "\"Neighbors called about a smell and constant crying for about a week. One neighbor had pressed an ear to the window and heard the cats.\""), .direct("Who owns the house?", "\"{D}. Records show {DL} had lived there for years and had taken in animals for a long time, and was listed as a rescue contact.\""), .direct("What do the veterinary reports say?", "\"All thirty cats had dehydration, and several had signs of starvation. Four needed intensive care. The reports also noted ear mites and skin infections.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s earlier dealings with animal control?", "\"{D.He} had been told about conditions twice before. We had left notices both times that the house needed cleaning and more supervision.\""), .cross("{D} was in the hospital for ten days, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.his} hospital record shows an admission for ten days. We confirmed that after the cats were removed.\""), .cross("{D} told you a cousin was supposed to feed the cats, didn't {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} said so. We contacted the cousin, who said {D.he} had never been asked to feed them.\""), .cross("{D} took in the cats to help them, correct?", "\"As far as we know, yes. {D.He} was not running a business. The intent seems to have been to care for animals that had nowhere else to go.\""), .cross("Some of the cats were in better shape than others, weren't they?", "\"Yes. A few were stable and several were fine after fluids. Four were close to death, and that was the worst of it.\""), .cross("You do not know how long the cats had gone without food and water, do you?", "\"Not exactly. The veterinarian estimated several days. The neighbors reported crying for about a week, so it could have been longer.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} let thirty cats go without food and water.", "A caretaker who was in the hospital."),
        allocution: "\"I'm not proud of it, Your Honor.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been told about the conditions twice before the hospital stay.", "The cousin says {D.he} was never asked to feed them."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you in the hospital when the cats were found?", "\"Yes. I went in with chest pain and was kept ten days. I could not call anyone because I was sick and my phone was at home.\""), .direct("Who was supposed to feed the cats while you were gone?", "\"A cousin who has a key. I told the cousin I was going in and asked if {D.he} could stop by. I thought we had an agreement.\""), .direct("Why did you take in so many cats?", "\"They were strays, and people dropped them at my door. I could not turn them away. I told myself I could manage until I got help.\""), .direct("What were the cats like before you went in?", "\"They were fed and watered every day. I kept the rooms closed to keep the cats from fighting, and I cleaned the boxes when I could.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned about the cats?", "\"I was heartbroken. I asked how they were and whether any could be saved. I signed them over so they could get proper care.\""), .direct("What do you want people to understand about what happened?", "\"I loved them. I did not abandon them on purpose. I was sick and I trusted someone who did not follow through.\""), .cross("The cousin says nobody asked {D.him} to feed them, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what the cousin says now. I believe I asked, and I may not have been clear while I was in pain.\""), .cross("You were warned twice about the house before the hospital, weren't you?", "\"Yes, and I was behind. I meant to clean and get help, and I let it go too long.\""), .cross("You kept thirty cats in closed rooms, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I knew it was too many. I did not see how else to keep them safe from each other, and I should have asked for help.\""), .cross("You did not arrange a backup for the cats in writing, did you?", "\"No. I should have written it down and given a second person a key, and I did not.\""), .cross("Four cats nearly died, and that happened on your watch, didn't it?", "\"Yes, they were my cats and I take responsibility. I wish I had done more to make sure they had help before I went in.\"")],
        openings: ("Neighbors reported a smell and a week of crying. Officers found thirty cats in closed rooms with no water, empty bowls, and litter piled on the floors. Four were near death.", "{D} was in the hospital for ten days and trusted a cousin to feed the cats. The cousin did not follow through. That is a tragedy, not a crime of cruelty."),
        closings: ("Thirty cats, no water, no food, and conditions {D} had been warned about twice. A hospital stay explains where {D} was, but not why no one was in charge of the animals.", "{D} was in the hospital, asked a cousin to help, and loved the animals. No one wanted the cats to suffer, and {D} did not neglect them on purpose."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{D} is warned about conditions."), (-10, "{D} enters the hospital."), (0, "Neighbors call animal control."), (0, "The cats are removed."), (1, "The veterinary findings.")],
        identified: "Animal control's report.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["necessity"])

    static let deadBrotherIdentityV1 = SmallCases.make(
