        state: [E(.document, 3, "Loan Application", "{V}'s identity and an address near {D}'s."), E(.document, 3, "Death Record", "{V} died three years earlier."), E(.digital, 2, "Phone Log", "Calls to the bank from {D}'s phone.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Family Consent", "{DL} says a relative said it was fine.")],
        role: "Bank fraud investigator",
        exam: [.direct("Whose identity was used on the loan application?", "\"{V}'s name, Social Security number and birth date. {V} died of a heart attack three years ago, and the death record is on file.\""), .direct("What was the loan for and how much was it?", "\"A $34,000 car loan, plus two credit cards opened in the same name over the next eighteen months. The applications used an address near {D}'s.\""), .direct("What did your investigation show about the phone calls to the bank?", "\"Several calls to the bank about the account came from a phone registered to {D.him}. The calls asked about payments and balances.\""), .direct("Who received the car purchased with the loan?", "\"{DL}. The dealer's records show {DL} signed the paperwork and took the keys. The signature on the application was a scrawl that did not match {V}'s.\""), .direct("How was the fraud discovered?", "\"The bank's monitoring flagged an account in the name of a deceased person. I pulled the records and called the number on file, which rang {D.his} phone.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you when you called?", "\"{D.He} said a relative had given permission. We then contacted that relative, who said no one had been given permission to use the identity.\""), .cross("The signature on the application is a scrawl, isn't it?", "\"It is, and it is not clearly {DL}'s. I cannot say who signed it. The handwriting was too loose for me to identify.\""), .cross("{D} was honest with you about taking the loan, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} did not deny that {D.he} took the loan. {D.he} said it was done with permission, and {D.he} was direct about that.\""), .cross("The car was financed in a family member's name, wasn't it?", "\"In a deceased family member's name, yes. That is what makes this unusual. The person who died was a sibling of {DL}.\""), .cross("You never spoke to {V}, did you?", "\"No. {V} died three years ago. I reviewed the records, the bank applications, and the phone logs. I could not interview {V}.\""), .cross("The relative who denied giving permission could be mistaken, couldn't the relative?", "\"I cannot rule that out. I can say the relative told me clearly that no permission was given. I recorded that in my report.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a dead sibling's identity to borrow money.", "A relative's permission."),
