        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Curb Find", "{DL} says the set was at the curb."), E(.statement, 1, "No Label", "{DL} says nothing marked it as the church's.")],
        role: "Church secretary",
        exam: [.direct("What was taken from the church lawn?", "\"A wooden nativity set and a lighted sleigh. Together they were worth about $410, and the church had put them out the week before Christmas for the community.\""), .direct("What did the security camera on the fellowship hall record?", "\"A pickup with a trailer pulled up to the lawn at 3 a.m. on {DATE}. People loaded figures onto the trailer and drove away within a few minutes.\""), .direct("How did the church learn who might have the set?", "\"A deputy found the nativity figures leaning against a wall in {D}'s barn. The figures had the church's stencil marked on the back.\""), .direct("What is the stencil on the figures?", "\"A small mark our building committee painted on the back of each piece when we made them. It reads with our church's initials and a year.\""), .direct("How does the church put out its decorations?", "\"Volunteers set them up on the lawn after Thanksgiving and take them in after Epiphany. Nothing is ever put at the curb or given away.\""), .direct("What did the church do after the set went missing?", "\"We checked the lawn and the shed and told the sheriff's office. We also looked at the camera, and the church put out a notice to members.\""), .cross("The stencil on the back is small, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is about the size of a coin. You would have to turn a figure around to see it, and it is not obvious from the front.\""), .cross("The lawn is at a roadside, correct?", "\"Yes, it is near the road for visibility. People drive by it every day and many stop to take photographs.\""), .cross("You do not know where {D} was at 3 a.m., do you?", "\"I know what the camera shows. A pickup and trailer stopped, and I cannot see who was driving or tell you where the driver was before.\""), .cross("A nativity set could look discarded in bad weather, couldn't it?", "\"If it had fallen over, perhaps. But ours was upright and anchored with stakes. It did not look abandoned to anyone who looked at it.\""), .cross("Someone from the church spoke to the defendant about the set before the theft, didn't they?", "\"I understand a member was asked about buying it. I did not take part in that conversation, and I do not know what was said.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a church's nativity set at night.", "A finder who thought it was thrown out."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} took the sleigh too, though the sleigh was not at the curb.", "{DL} had asked a church member about buying the set."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the nativity set from the church lawn?", "\"I picked it up, yes. I was driving by early in the morning and saw it by the road. I thought someone had put it out for pickup.\""), .direct("Why were you out at 3 a.m.?", "\"I work odd hours hauling hay and equipment. I was heading home with my trailer when I saw the set in my headlights.\""), .direct("Why did you think it was thrown away?", "\"It was near the road, and nobody was around. I have seen people leave old decorations at the curb for trash day, so I did not think twice.\""), .direct("What did you do with the figures after you loaded them?", "\"I put them in my barn. I planned to ask around to see whether anyone wanted them, and I did not think about it again until a deputy came.\""), .direct("Why did you take the sleigh as well?", "\"It was close, and it looked like part of the same display. I thought they went together and that someone would want them as a set.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy asked about it?", "\"I showed the deputy the figures in my barn right away. I did not move them or hide anything, and I told the deputy where I had found them.\""), .cross("The sleigh was not at the curb, was it?", "\"No, it was a little back from the road. I should have noticed that it did not look like trash, and I did not.\""), .cross("You asked a member of the church about buying the set before, didn't you?", "\"I did. I asked, and the person said it was not for sale. I changed my mind about it, and I never asked again.\""), .cross("You drove a pickup with a trailer at 3 a.m. to pick up a curb find, didn't you?", "\"I drive a trailer for work. I do not think of it as unusual. I understand how it looks on a camera at that hour.\""), .cross("The figures had a stencil on the back, and you did not look, did you?", "\"No, I did not turn them over. I picked them up and put them on the trailer. If I had looked, I would have known.\""), .cross("You took a decorated set from a church lawn in the week before Christmas, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have checked with someone first. I regret the harm it caused, and I wish I had left it where it was.\"")],
        openings: ("A nativity set and a lighted sleigh vanished from a church lawn at 3 a.m. A camera caught a pickup and trailer, and a deputy found the figures in {D}'s barn with the church's stencil.", "{D} saw the set at the curb and thought it had been thrown away. It was an honest mistake by a hay hauler on the road at night, not a theft."),
        closings: ("The camera, the stencil on the back of the figures, and the figures in {D}'s barn all tie {D} to the theft. {D} had even asked about buying the set before taking it.", "{D} saw something at the curb, loaded it, and never hid it. A deputy found it in plain sight, and {D} told the deputy exactly where it came from."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{D} asks about buying the set."), (0, "3 a.m.: the pickup stops."), (0, "7 a.m.: the church finds the lawn bare."), (1, "The camera is reviewed."), (2, "A deputy visits {D}'s barn.")],
        identified: "A security camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let poisonedNeighborDogsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.poisonedNeighborDogs",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Pasture Goats Found Dead After Rat Poison Tossed in Their Feed Bin", "Fence-Line Quarrel Precedes the Deaths"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Maliciously killed animals belonging to {V} by poison, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} found two goats dead in a pasture on {DATE} and a third sick. A veterinarian found rat poison in the feed bin and in the animals. For months {V} and {D}, who owns the lot next door, had argued over a fence line and a gate. A trail camera showed someone at the feed bin before dawn. Hardware store records showed {D} bought rat poison three days earlier. {DL} says {D.he} has rats of {D.his} own and that anyone could have reached the bin.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Veterinary Report", "Anticoagulant poison in the goats and in the feed."), E(.document, 2, "Hardware Receipt", "{D} bought the same brand three days earlier."), E(.video, 2, "Trail Camera", "A figure at the feed bin before dawn."), E(.physical, 1, "Feed Bin", "Poison pellets mixed into the feed.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Rats at Home", "{DL} says {D.he} bought it for rats."), E(.statement, 1, "Open Pasture", "The gate is never locked.")],
        role: "Veterinarian",
        exam: [.direct("What did your examination of the goats show?", "\"Anticoagulant rodent poison in the blood and stomach contents of both goats that died, and in the third goat that was sick. The same poison was in the feed.\""), .direct("How was the poison delivered to the animals?", "\"It was mixed into the feed bin. We found poison pellets among the feed grains, and the feed in the sealed bags at the back of the barn was clean.\""), .direct("How quickly does that kind of poison work?", "\"It prevents blood from clotting, so animals bleed internally over several days. It takes repeated feedings, which fits the feed bin being tampered with.\""), .direct("What did you do for the sick goat?", "\"I gave it vitamin K and supportive care and monitored it for a week. It survived, though it was weak for some time.\""), .direct("How many animals were affected in total?", "\"Three goats. Two died in the pasture and one became ill. We found no signs of poisoning in the other animals on the property.\""), .direct("What can you say about the brand of poison in the feed?", "\"It was the same brand and formulation sold at the hardware store where {D} bought rat poison three days before. The pellets were a distinctive blue.\""), .cross("Rat poison is common on farms, isn't it?", "\"Yes, it is very common. Many farms use it, and several brands are almost identical in composition.\""), .cross("The feed in the bags was clean, wasn't it?", "\"The sealed feed bags tested clean. Only the feed in the open bin had poison, which is why I think someone added it there.\""), .cross("Anyone could have reached the feed bin, couldn't they?", "\"The bin sits in an open pasture and the gate is never locked, so access was not controlled. I cannot say who reached it.\""), .cross("You cannot tell the jury who put the poison in the bin, can you?", "\"No. I can tell you what was in the animals and in the feed. I cannot say who put it there.\""), .cross("The blue pellets are used by many people, aren't they?", "\"They are one of the most widely sold types. I cannot say that one purchase links to this bin by itself.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} poisoned a neighbor's goats over a fence line.", "A neighbor with rats of {D.his} own."),
        allocution: "\"I lost my temper, and I'm sorry for what I did.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had said {V}'s animals 'would not be a problem much longer'.", "{DL}'s property has no rat poison left in the bait station."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you poison your neighbor's goats?", "\"No. I did not touch those goats or that feed. I argued with my neighbor about the fence, but I would never hurt an animal.\""), .direct("Why did you buy rat poison three days before the goats died?", "\"I have rats in my own barn and had seen droppings along the wall. I bought a box to set out, and I used part of it in a bait station.\""), .direct("What do you have left of what you bought?", "\"Very little. I put it in the bait station and the rest went into a bag in the barn. The deputy checked and found the bait station empty.\""), .direct("What was the argument with {V} about?", "\"A fence line and a gate. We could not agree where the boundary ran. It had gone on for months, and we were both frustrated.\""), .direct("Where were you the morning the goats were poisoned?", "\"At home, asleep. I get up early, but I stay in my own yard. I did not walk over to {V}'s pasture that morning.\""), .direct("How did you feel when you learned about the goats?", "\"Terrible. I felt sick, and I also knew people would suspect me because of the argument. I had nothing to do with it.\""), .cross("You said {V}'s animals would not be a problem much longer, didn't you?", "\"I said something like that out of frustration. I meant the argument about the fence would be over soon, not that anyone would be hurt.\""), .cross("You did not report any poison missing, did you?", "\"No. I used the rest of it. I did not keep a count, and I had nothing to report.\""), .cross("You bought the same brand that killed the goats, correct?", "\"I did buy that brand. It is the one sold at the nearby store, and I did not choose it for any reason.\""), .cross("The bait station on your property was empty, wasn't it?", "\"It was, because rats had taken the bait. I understand that looks odd, but that is what I saw when I checked.\""), .cross("You and {V} had argued for months, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, we had. It was a hard dispute, and I was angry about it. But being angry is not the same as poisoning an animal.\"")],
        openings: ("Two goats died in a pasture and a third nearly did. A veterinarian found rat poison in their feed, a camera showed a figure at the bin, and {D} had bought the same poison days before.", "{D} had rats of {D.his} own and bought a common poison for them. The pasture gate is never locked, and anyone could have reached that bin."),
        closings: ("Same poison, same brand, a neighbor feud, and a threat that {V}'s animals would 'not be a problem much longer.' These facts point to one person.", "Rat poison is sold in every farm store, the gate was open, and no one saw {D} at the bin. A feud is not proof, and a receipt is not proof."),
        timeline: [(-90, "The fence-line quarrel begins."), (-3, "{D} buys rat poison."), (0, "Before dawn: a figure at the bin."), (0, "{V} finds the goats."), (1, "The veterinarian's finding.")],
        identified: "A veterinary report.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let auntPowerOfAttorneyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.auntPowerOfAttorney",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Relative With Power of Attorney Charged After Elderly Aunt's Savings Drop by $140,000", "Pickup Truck and Transfers in Nephew's Name"],
        law: "exploitationElder",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Being in a position of trust and confidence with {V}, an older adult, knowingly by deception used {V}'s funds for {D.his} own benefit, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 35...62,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, 88, signed a power of attorney naming {D} after a fall two years ago. Over nineteen months $140,600 left {V}'s savings, including $62,000 for a pickup truck titled to {D} and $38,000 in transfers to {D}'s account. {DL} says {V} approved each spending and the truck was for driving {V} to appointments.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Records", "$140,600 moved out of {V}'s savings."), E(.document, 3, "Vehicle Title", "A pickup titled to {D} for $62,000."), E(.document, 2, "Adult Protective Report", "{V} was confused about the money.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Approval", "{DL} says {V} approved each expense.")],
        role: "Adult Protective Services social worker",
        exam: [.direct("What did you learn about {V}'s financial situation when you opened your investigation?", "\"{V} is 88 and had a savings account that lost $140,600 over nineteen months. {V} could tell me little about where the money had gone.\""), .direct("What is a power of attorney, and who held {V}'s?", "\"It lets someone manage another person's finances. {V} signed one naming {D} after a fall two years ago. It requires the agent to act in the principal's interest.\""), .direct("What did the bank records show?", "\"Regular withdrawals and transfers out of savings, including $62,000 toward a pickup truck titled to {D.him} and $38,000 moved into {D.his} own account.\""), .direct("How did {V} appear when you spoke with {V}?", "\"Confused about the money. {V} could not say what was spent, what was left, or what the truck was for, and became upset when I asked.\""), .direct("What records did {D} provide to show how the money was spent?", "\"None. There was no ledger, no receipts, and no written approval from {V}. {DL} said everything had been agreed verbally.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the pickup truck?", "\"It was titled to {D.him}, not to {V}. We found no sign that it was used to drive {V} to appointments, and {V}'s neighbors said they never saw it.\""), .cross("{V} did sign the power of attorney willingly, didn't {V}?", "\"Yes. It was signed after a fall, with a witness, and {V} understood who was being named. I have no reason to think it was forged.\""), .cross("A power of attorney allows the agent to spend on the principal's care, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. It allows reasonable expenses for the principal's benefit. It does not allow the agent to buy a truck for the agent's own use.\""), .cross("{V} told you in general terms that the defendant had helped, didn't {V}?", "\"{V} said {DL} helped and was kind. {V} did not say {V.he} had agreed to every expense, and could not name any specific purchase.\""), .cross("Some of the withdrawals were for {V}'s own care, weren't they?", "\"Some may have been. I could not identify which ones without receipts. That is part of the problem with the lack of any ledger.\""), .cross("You did not interview the defendant's other relatives, did you?", "\"I interviewed those I could reach. They did not have information about the spending, and none of them had been shown any records.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a relative's savings for {D.himself}.", "A caregiver with permission."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry to everyone I let down. I'll repay what I can.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} never kept receipts or a ledger.", "The truck was never used to drive {V}."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take money from {V}'s savings?", "\"I spent money from the account, yes. I believed {V} had approved each expense. I was helping {V} manage everything after the fall.\""), .direct("What was the pickup truck for?", "\"I told {V} I needed a reliable truck to drive to appointments and carry supplies. {V} said that was fine and agreed to the purchase.\""), .direct("Did you drive {V} to appointments in the truck?", "\"Some. Mostly I used it to haul things and to run errands. I did not keep track of how often I drove {V} anywhere.\""), .direct("Why did you move $38,000 to your own account?", "\"I told myself it was for reimbursement and for my time. {V} had said I deserved to be paid for the work I was doing.\""), .direct("How did you track what you spent?", "\"I did not. I assumed I could remember it, and I did not keep a ledger or receipts. That was a mistake, and I know it.\""), .direct("What was your relationship with {V}?", "\"{V} is a close relative. I took on a lot after the fall. I cooked, drove, paid bills and handled everything, and I believed I was doing it out of love.\""), .cross("You never kept receipts, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I did not think I would need them. {V} trusted me, and I thought that was enough.\""), .cross("The truck was never used to take {V} to appointments, was it?", "\"Not often. I used it for my own errands, and I did not use it as I said I would.\""), .cross("You took $38,000 for yourself in nineteen months, didn't you?", "\"It was moved to my account. I called it reimbursement, but I did not get anyone to approve it in writing.\""), .cross("A power of attorney does not authorize you to pay yourself, does it?", "\"Not without clear permission. I did not have it in writing, and I understand why that is a serious problem.\""), .cross("{V} was confused about the money, wasn't {V}?", "\"{V} gets confused sometimes. I should have taken that more seriously and kept proper records so no one could say I took advantage.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, who is 88, named {D} in a power of attorney after a fall. Over nineteen months $140,600 left {V}'s savings, including $62,000 for a truck titled to {D} and $38,000 sent to {D}'s account.", "{D} cared for {V} after a fall and believed {V} approved each expense. The mistake was poor record-keeping, not a plan to steal."),
        closings: ("$140,600 gone, a truck in {D}'s name, and no ledger, no receipts, and no written approval. A power of attorney is a duty to protect, not a license to spend.", "{D} was the person who showed up for {V} after the fall. Poor paperwork is not theft, and {V} agreed in general to {D}'s help."),
        timeline: [(-570, "The power of attorney."), (-300, "The truck."), (0, "A bank flags the account."), (30, "Adult protective services visits.")],
        identified: "Bank records and a title.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "victimRights"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let selfCheckoutBananaV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.selfCheckoutBanana",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Loss Prevention Notes Shopper Scanning One Pack of Razor Blades and Bagging Four", "Pattern Across Seven Visits Documented"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole $94 in merchandise from a retail store by failing to scan items at self-checkout, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A big-box store's loss prevention officer watched {D} at self-checkout on {DATE} scan a single pack of razor blades and bag four. The cart's contents did not match the receipt. Records and camera footage showed seven similar visits in two months. The total was $94 on this visit. {DL} says the machine did not register the items and {D.he} never noticed.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Self-Checkout Camera", "{D} scans one pack and bags four."), E(.document, 2, "Receipts", "Seven receipts that omit items in the cart."), E(.document, 1, "Prior Visits", "Footage of six earlier visits.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Machine Did Not Register", "{DL} says the machine did not register the items."), E(.statement, 1, "Didn't Notice", "{DL} says {D.he} never noticed.")],
        role: "Retail loss prevention officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on the self-checkout camera on {DATE}?", "\"{D} scanned a single pack of razor blades and then bagged four packs. The cart's contents did not match what was scanned or paid for.\""), .direct("How did you notice the pattern at the kiosk?", "\"Our system flagged a mismatch between the cart weight and scans. I pulled up the camera and watched {DL} place items into the bag without scanning them.\""), .direct("How many similar visits did you find?", "\"Seven in two months. I went back through footage from the other visits and found the same method on each one.\""), .direct("What was the loss on this visit?", "\"$94. On each visit, the loss was small, but I counted the total across seven visits and it added up to several hundred dollars.\""), .direct("Which kiosk did {D} use?", "\"The same one each time, at the end of the row, away from the attendant's station. It has a clear view of the exit, but a poor view of the attendant.\""), .direct("What item was scanned each time?", "\"The cheapest item in the cart. The other items went into the bag without a scan, and the receipt listed only that one cheap item.\""), .cross("The self-checkout machines sometimes miss scans, don't they?", "\"Yes, they do. Machines sometimes fail to register an item. That is why I looked at footage and not just the receipts.\""), .cross("{D} did not try to hide the bag from the camera, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D.He} bagged items in plain view. I cannot say whether {D.he} thought the camera was not recording.\""), .cross("You did not stop {D} the day of the visit, did you?", "\"I let the visit finish so I could review the video. We stopped {D.him} at the door and asked about the unscanned items.\""), .cross("{D} did not run when you stopped {D.him}, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D.He} stood still and listened. {D.he} said the machine had not registered the items, and {D.he} had not noticed.\""), .cross("Many shoppers do not check their receipt, do they?", "\"Many do not, no. I would not say failing to check a receipt is a crime by itself. I focus on the repeated pattern.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bagged items without scanning them.", "A shopper who trusted a machine."),
        allocution: "\"I wasn't thinking about the person on the other end. I am now.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} always chose the same kiosk away from the attendant.", "{DL} always scanned the cheapest item."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you skip scanning items on purpose?", "\"No. I scanned everything I could see. The machine did not beep on some items, and I assumed they had registered.\""), .direct("Why did you use the kiosk by the door?", "\"It is close to the exit and usually empty. I use it because I am often in a hurry, not because of the attendant.\""), .direct("Did you look at your receipt after the purchase?", "\"I did not. I take the receipt and put it in my bag, and I do not usually read it. I trusted the machine to be accurate.\""), .direct("What did you buy on that visit?", "\"Razor blades, some household items and a few groceries. I scanned the blades once, and then I scanned a few others.\""), .direct("What did you do when the loss prevention officer stopped you?", "\"I stood still and answered every question. I told the officer I had not noticed anything wrong, and I offered to pay for anything missing.\""), .direct("What did you buy on the other visits, as best you recall?", "\"The same sort of things: razor blades, laundry supplies, a few snacks. I came in when I ran low, and I bought the same items each time.\""), .cross("You scanned only the cheapest item on seven visits, didn't you?", "\"The receipts show that. It looks bad, but I did not choose the cheapest item on purpose. It happened to be the first thing in the cart.\""), .cross("You used the same kiosk every time, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It is near the door and I am a creature of habit. I did not choose it because of the attendant.\""), .cross("Seven visits is a lot of times for a machine to miss items, isn't it?", "\"I know. I do not understand why it kept happening. I never checked my receipt, and I should have.\""), .cross("You bagged four packs and scanned one, didn't you?", "\"That is what the video shows. I did not realize I had only scanned one. I trusted the machine to tell me if something was wrong.\""), .cross("You did not report any problem with the machine, did you?", "\"No. I did not think there was a problem until I was stopped. I should have been more careful.\"")],
        openings: ("A loss prevention officer watched {D} scan one pack of razor blades and bag four. The same pattern showed up on seven visits in two months, always at the same kiosk.", "{D} trusted a self-checkout machine and never checked a receipt. Machines miss scans, and that is a store problem, not a crime."),
        closings: ("One scan, four bagged, seven visits, the same kiosk, and the same cheap item scanned each time. That is a pattern and not a malfunction.", "{D} did not hide the bag, did not run, and offered to pay. A machine that misses items and a shopper who does not check a receipt do not add up to theft."),
        timeline: [(-60, "The first visit."), (-14, "The officer notices the pattern."), (0, "The officer watches the checkout."), (0, "{D} is stopped at the door."), (1, "A summons is issued.")],
        identified: "A self-checkout camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let neighborCarGarageBurnV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.neighborCarGarageBurn",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Hay Barn and Tractor Destroyed in Predawn Fire After Years of Property-Line Quarrel", "Fuel Can Found in Ditch Matches Gas Station Receipt"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a barn owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A hay barn and tractor burned before dawn on {DATE}. {V} and {D}, neighbors, had argued for years about a property line and a drainage ditch. A red fuel can was found in the ditch. A gas station receipt from two days earlier showed {D} buying the same type of can and ten dollars of fuel. A trail camera captured a vehicle slowing near the barn at 3:50 a.m. {DL} says the can was left in {D}'s truck bed and stolen.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Marshal", "Fuel poured along the east wall."), E(.document, 3, "Gas Station Receipt", "{D} buys the same can and fuel."), E(.video, 2, "Trail Camera", "A vehicle slows near the barn at 3:50 a.m."), E(.physical, 1, "Fuel Can", "A red can found in the ditch.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Stolen Can", "{DL} says the can was stolen from the truck."), E(.statement, 1, "At Home", "{DL} says {D.he} was asleep.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("Where did the fire begin in the barn?", "\"Along the east wall. The burn pattern showed fuel poured along the base of the wall and ignited, and the fire climbed quickly toward the hay.\""), .direct("What did you find in the ditch?", "\"A red fuel can, partly melted, lying near the property line. It was empty, and it carried a strong smell of gasoline.\""), .direct("What did the gas station receipt show?", "\"{D} bought a red fuel can of the same type and ten dollars of gasoline two days before the fire. The receipt is time-stamped and the clerk remembered the sale.\""), .direct("What did the trail camera show?", "\"A vehicle slowing near the barn at 3:50 in the morning. It was a pickup with a ladder rack, and it matched the type of truck {DL} drives.\""), .direct("What was lost in the fire?", "\"A hay barn and a tractor parked inside it. {V} also lost stored hay for the winter, so the damage was well beyond the building.\""), .direct("What can you say about how long the fire burned?", "\"It burned until well after dawn. Firefighters arrived about twenty minutes after the first call, and the roof had already begun to fall.\""), .cross("No fingerprints were found on the fuel can, were they?", "\"None usable, no. The can was damaged by the heat and the dirt in the ditch, so I could not recover a print.\""), .cross("Red fuel cans are sold in every hardware store, aren't they?", "\"Yes. They are one of the most common cans sold. I cannot tell you where this particular can was bought.\""), .cross("The trail camera does not show the driver, does it?", "\"No. It shows a vehicle at night. The image is dark, and I cannot read the plate or identify anyone inside.\""), .cross("You do not know who poured the fuel, do you?", "\"I know it was poured and lit. I cannot say who did it from the burn pattern alone.\""), .cross("Many trucks look like the one on the trail camera, don't they?", "\"Many pickups share that profile. I cannot say with certainty that the truck on the camera is {DL}'s.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned a neighbor's barn after years of quarrelling.", "A neighbor whose can was stolen."),
        allocution: "\"I'm not proud of it, Your Honor.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} never reported the can stolen.", "{DL}'s truck matches the vehicle on the trail camera."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you set fire to {V}'s barn?", "\"No. I did not. {V} and I had a long argument over a property line, but I would never burn a barn full of hay.\""), .direct("What was the can you bought two days before?", "\"I bought it to carry fuel for my mower and a generator. I left it in the bed of my truck afterward, and I did not think about it again.\""), .direct("What happened to the can after you bought it?", "\"It disappeared from my truck bed. I noticed it was gone the next day, and I figured it had been taken. I did not report it.\""), .direct("Where were you at 3:50 the morning of the fire?", "\"At home, asleep in my own bed. I live alone, so nobody can say that, but I did not leave the house that night.\""), .direct("What do you drive?", "\"A pickup with a ladder rack for work. Plenty of people in the county drive something similar, and I had no reason to be near {V}'s barn.\""), .direct("How do you feel about the fire?", "\"Awful. It was a terrible loss for {V}. I felt sick about it, and I knew that people would think I had something to do with it.\""), .cross("You did not report the can as stolen, did you?", "\"No. I did not think about it until the deputy asked. It was a cheap can, and I did not think a theft report would matter.\""), .cross("The truck on the trail camera matches yours, doesn't it?", "\"It looks similar. A lot of trucks look like that one. I was not driving it that night.\""), .cross("You and {V} had argued for years about the property line, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. We argued over the line and a drainage ditch. It was bitter at times, and I was angry, but I did not burn anything.\""), .cross("You bought a can and fuel two days before the fire, didn't you?", "\"I did, for my mower. I understand how that looks next to what happened, and I wish I had not bought it that week.\""), .cross("The can was found in the ditch between your property and {V}'s, wasn't it?", "\"I was told that, but I never put it there myself. Someone could have taken it from my truck and left it there.\"")],
        openings: ("A hay barn and a tractor burned before dawn. A red fuel can was found in the ditch, a receipt showed {D} had bought the same can two days earlier, and a trail camera caught a pickup near the barn.", "{D} bought a can for a mower, had it taken from a truck bed, and slept at home. Anyone could have used a cheap can to start that fire."),
        closings: ("Years of quarrelling, the same type of can bought two days before, and a truck like {D}'s on camera at 3:50 in the morning. The pieces fit.", "A can, a receipt, and a truck that looks like many others. Nobody saw {D} at the barn, and a feud is not proof of arson."),
        timeline: [(-730, "The property-line quarrel begins."), (-2, "{D} buys the can."), (0, "3:50 a.m.: the truck passes the trail camera."), (0, "4:30 a.m.: the barn is found burning."), (1, "The marshal's findings.")],
        identified: "A fire marshal's report.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let cattleAuctionV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.cattleAuction",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Livestock Market Sale Draws Complaint From Neighbor Missing Twenty-Two Head", "Brand Records Don't Match Seller"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Knowingly and designedly, with intent to cheat and defraud, obtained $26,950 from a livestock market by falsely representing that cattle belonged to {D.him}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 28...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} leased pasture next to {D}'s land and ran 40 head there. On {DATE}, {D} hauled 22 of them to a livestock market and sold them for $26,950, signing a form swearing the cattle were {D.his}. The brands did not match. {DL} says the cattle wandered onto {D.his} land and {D.he} thought they were strays given to {D.him}.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Sale Form", "{D} swears the cattle are {D.his}."), E(.document, 3, "Brand Records", "The brands belong to {V}."), E(.statement, 2, "Auction Clerk", "{D} hauled 22 head alone.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Strays", "{DL} says the cattle wandered onto {D.his} land.")],
        role: "Cattle owner",
        exam: [.direct("How many cattle do you run on the leased pasture beside {D}'s land?", "\"Forty head. I lease the pasture from the landowner and keep them there through the summer. I check them at least twice a week and count them each time.\""), .direct("What did you discover missing on {DATE}?", "\"Twenty-two head were gone. I counted twice, walked the fence line, and found tire tracks and a section of wire pulled down near the gate on {D}'s side.\""), .direct("How are your cattle identified?", "\"Each one carries my registered brand on the left hip. The brand is on file with the state, and I have the paperwork and photographs of every animal.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the sale?", "\"A livestock market in the next county sold 22 head that day for $26,950. {D.He} signed the form swearing the cattle belonged to {D.him}.\""), .direct("What did the brands show when the market inspected them?", "\"They were my brand, clear on every animal. The inspector's notes list my brand for all 22, and the market held the check.\""), .direct("What did the auction clerk tell you about the delivery?", "\"That {D.he} hauled all 22 head alone, in one load, and signed the paperwork at the window. No one else came with the trailer.\""), .cross("Cattle do sometimes wander through fences, don't they?", "\"Sometimes they do, yes. That is why I check the fence. A few might wander, but not 22 at once into a neighbor's trailer.\""), .cross("The fence between the properties was only partly up, wasn't it?", "\"It was in some disrepair along one stretch. That is the stretch where the wire was pulled down, and the cut ends were clean.\""), .cross("You cannot say how the cattle got onto the defendant's land, can you?", "\"I did not see it. I know they were on my lease the day before and on a trailer to market the next day.\""), .cross("Brands can fade, can't they?", "\"Some do on old animals. These were clear. The inspector read them without difficulty, and I have photographs from this spring.\""), .cross("{D} did not hide the sale, did {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} sold at a public market and signed a form. I cannot say what {D.he} was thinking, but the paperwork says the cattle were {D.his}.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold a neighbor's cattle as {D.his} own.", "Strays on {D.his} land."),
        allocution: "\"I should have told the truth the first time.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} loaded them at night.", "{DL} paid a hauler cash and said nothing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you sell the 22 head of cattle at the livestock market?", "\"Yes. I hauled them there and signed the form. I believed they were strays that had come onto my land and that I was entitled to them.\""), .direct("Why did you think they were yours?", "\"They had been on my land for a few days. Nobody claimed them, and an old neighbor once told me that strays that stay on your land become yours.\""), .direct("Why did you load the cattle at night?", "\"It was cooler for the animals, and the heat was bad that week. I have always hauled at night in the summer to keep them from stressing.\""), .direct("Did you look at the brands before you loaded them?", "\"I glanced at a few. They were faded in the dim light, and I did not know whose brand it was. I did not check the records.\""), .direct("How did you get the cattle to the market?", "\"I paid a hauler with a big trailer to take them. I paid cash and rode along, and I did not tell the hauler where the cattle came from.\""), .direct("What did you do when {V} called you about it?", "\"I said I thought they were mine and offered to talk. I wanted to find out what had happened and who really owned them.\""), .cross("You signed a form under oath that the cattle were yours, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. I believed it at the time, but I did not check, and I see now that I should have.\""), .cross("You paid a hauler cash and said nothing to anyone, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It is how I usually pay for hauling. I did not think it was unusual, but I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("The brands on all 22 head belonged to {V}, didn't they?", "\"Yes, I learned that afterward. I did not know it when I loaded them, and I did not look closely.\""), .cross("You never called {V} or the sheriff to ask about strays, did you?", "\"No. I should have. I did not know how to find the owner, and I made a mistake in assuming they were free for the taking.\""), .cross("You kept the $26,950, didn't you?", "\"The market held the check once the brands were questioned. I did not get to keep it, and I did not try to cash it.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} leased pasture next to {D} and lost 22 head of cattle in a single night. {D} sold them for $26,950 at a livestock market and signed a form swearing they were {D.his}.", "{D} thought a group of strays on {D.his} land had been left for the taking. It was a mistake about the brands, not a plan to steal a neighbor's herd."),
        closings: ("Every animal carried {V}'s brand. {D} loaded them at night, paid a hauler cash, and signed a sworn form claiming the cattle. That is theft.", "{D} did not hide the sale. {D} took the cattle to a public market and signed a form in plain view. That is how an honest mistake looks."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The cattle go missing."), (0, "The sale."), (7, "{V} notices."), (14, "Market records are pulled.")],
        identified: "Brand records and a sale form.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "mistakeOfFact", "justification"])

    static let foundPhoneSoldV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.foundPhoneSold",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Phone Left on Gym Bench Taken to Repair Kiosk for Unlock, Owner's Tracker Led to the Counter", "Kiosk Work Order Lists Defendant's Name"],
        law: "possStolen",
        spec: "Possessed a cellular telephone valued at $540 belonging to {V}, knowing it stolen, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} left a phone on a gym bench on {DATE} and returned to find it gone. The gym camera showed {D} pocket it. Two days later {V}'s tracker showed the phone at a repair kiosk in a mall. The work order listed {D} asking for the phone to be unlocked and wiped. {DL} says {D.he} found the phone in the parking lot and wanted to find its owner.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Gym Camera", "{D} pockets a phone from the bench."), E(.document, 3, "Work Order", "{D} asks for a code removal and wipe."), E(.digital, 2, "Tracker Log", "The phone at the kiosk two days later.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Parking Lot", "{DL} says {D.he} found it in the lot."), E(.statement, 1, "Meant to Find Owner", "{DL} says {D.he} planned to find the owner.")],
        role: "Repair kiosk technician",
        exam: [.direct("What did {D} ask you to do with the phone?", "\"{D} asked me to remove the passcode and wipe the phone so it could be reset. {D.He} filled out a work order and said it was {D.his} own phone.\""), .direct("Did the defendant say who owned the phone?", "\"{DL} said it was {D.his}. I wrote it on the work order, and the phone's lock screen showed a name that was not {DL}'s.\""), .direct("How does your kiosk handle unlock requests?", "\"We ask for proof of ownership: a receipt, the original box, or an ID that matches the account. Without that, we do not unlock or wipe a phone.\""), .direct("What did the defendant offer as proof?", "\"Nothing. {D.He} said the phone was a gift and the receipt was lost. That did not satisfy our policy, so I stepped away to check the phone.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the phone that made you uneasy?", "\"It had a lock-screen message with another person's name and a notification from a gym app. The details did not match what {D.he} was telling me.\""), .direct("What did you do next?", "\"I told {DL} we would need a little time, and I called the sheriff's office from the back. Deputies arrived while {DL} was still waiting.\""), .cross("{D} did not run when you stepped away, did {D.he}?", "\"No. {D.He} stayed at the counter until the deputies arrived. {D.he} did not argue much, and I did not see any attempt to leave.\""), .cross("Plenty of people bring phones in to be unlocked, don't they?", "\"Yes, every day. Most have a receipt or can show the account. Some forget a passcode, and that is common.\""), .cross("{D} told you the phone was a gift, didn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {DL} said at the counter. The work order says the phone was {DL}'s. I did not know which version to believe.\""), .cross("You do not know how the defendant came to have the phone, do you?", "\"No. I only know what {D.he} told me and what the sheriff's report says. I cannot say how the phone left the gym.\""), .cross("Unlocking a phone is not illegal in itself, is it?", "\"No. It is a normal service when the person owns the phone. That is why we ask for proof of ownership first.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a phone and tried to have it wiped.", "A finder trying to find the owner."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} told the technician the phone was {D.his}.", "{DL} had taken a second phone from the gym a month before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the phone from the gym bench?", "\"I picked it up. I did not think of it as taking. It was sitting alone on a bench, and I was going to hand it to the front desk.\""), .direct("Where did you find the phone?", "\"In the gym, on a bench. I said the parking lot to the deputy, and that was wrong. I was nervous and I said the wrong thing.\""), .direct("Why did you take it to a repair kiosk?", "\"I could not unlock it to find the owner, and I thought a technician could. I did not know it would look like I was trying to steal it.\""), .direct("Why did you ask for a wipe?", "\"I wanted it reset so I could see a contact. I did not understand that a wipe would erase the owner's information.\""), .direct("Why did you tell the technician the phone was yours?", "\"I panicked. I thought the technician would not help if I said I had found it, and I said the first thing that came to mind.\""), .direct("What do you want {V} to know?", "\"That I am sorry for the stress. I never meant to keep the phone, and I should have handed it in at the desk.\""), .cross("You pocketed the phone on the gym camera, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I put it in my pocket. I meant to give it to the desk, and I kept it a lot longer than I meant to.\""), .cross("You told the technician the phone was yours, didn't you?", "\"I did. It was a lie, and I regret it. I was afraid of being accused.\""), .cross("Two days passed before you went to the kiosk, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I carried the phone for two days. I should have handed it in the same day, and I did not.\""), .cross("You had taken a second phone from the gym a month before, hadn't you?", "\"I had one in my bag that I found. I did not hand that one in, either. I should have handed in both.\""), .cross("You asked for the phone to be wiped, which would remove any way to find the owner, didn't you?", "\"I did, and I did not think about that. I wanted to get into it, and I wish I had thought it through.\"")],
        openings: ("A phone left on a gym bench was pocketed on camera, tracked two days later to a repair kiosk, and ordered unlocked and wiped. The work order is signed by {D}.", "{D} found a phone and tried to find its owner. {D} made some poor choices, but meant to return it, and that is not what a thief does."),
        closings: ("The gym camera, the tracker, and the work order tell one story: {D} took the phone, kept it two days, and asked for it to be wiped as {D.his} own.", "{D} found a phone and did not know how to find the owner. A scared answer to a technician is a mistake, not proof of theft."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 p.m.: the phone is left on the bench."), (0, "6:10 p.m.: {D} pockets it."), (2, "The phone reaches the kiosk."), (2, "The technician calls deputies."), (3, "{V}'s tracker is reviewed.")],
        identified: "A gym camera.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let warehouseInventoryBurnV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.warehouseInventoryBurn",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Furniture Showroom Fire Follows Removal of Best Stock to a Rented Unit", "Alarm Company Logs Camera System Disarmed Before Midnight"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a building owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A furniture showroom burned at night on {DATE}. {D}, the tenant, had moved the newest stock to a storage unit the week before. The alarm company's log showed the camera system was disarmed with {D}'s code at 11:48 p.m. The fire marshal found two points of origin and a space heater plugged into a power strip. {DL} says the heater started the fire and {D.he} moved stock because of a flood scare.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Marshal", "Two points of origin and an accelerant on the floor."), E(.digital, 3, "Alarm Log", "Cameras disarmed with {D}'s code at 11:48 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Storage Unit Rental", "Rented by {D} the week before the fire."), E(.document, 1, "Insurance", "Policy raised a month before.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Heater", "{DL} says a space heater started it."), E(.statement, 1, "Flood Scare", "{DL} says stock was moved over flood worries.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("How many points of origin did you find in the showroom?", "\"Two, in different parts of the floor, well apart from each other. Separate points of origin on a single floor are a sign the fire was set more than once.\""), .direct("What did you find on the floor at those points?", "\"An accelerant. The lab confirmed an ignitable liquid on the floor at both points, and the burn patterns matched a pour.\""), .direct("What did the alarm company log show?", "\"The camera system was disarmed using {D}'s code at 11:48 p.m. The fire alarm itself was triggered later, after the fire was well established.\""), .direct("What did the storage unit rental show?", "\"{D.He} rented a unit the week before the fire and moved the newest stock into it. Most of the pieces left in the showroom were older or damaged.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the insurance on the showroom?", "\"The policy had been raised about a month before the fire. The claim after the fire was based on the higher coverage.\""), .direct("What did you find about the space heater?", "\"A space heater was plugged into a power strip near one of the origins. It was heavily burned, but the pattern at that origin did not point to the heater.\""), .cross("A space heater and a power strip can start a fire, can't they?", "\"They can. That is why we looked at it. But the burn pattern and the lab results pointed to an ignitable liquid, not an electrical fault.\""), .cross("The area had a small flood history, didn't it?", "\"It had one small flood some years ago. It was minor, and the building was dry when we examined it.\""), .cross("You cannot say who set the fire, can you?", "\"No. I can tell you where and how it was started. The alarm log and the other evidence point to {D.him}, but I did not see who did it.\""), .cross("Raising insurance coverage is routine for a business, isn't it?", "\"It can be. Many businesses raise it each year. The timing here, a month before the fire, is what drew our attention.\""), .cross("Moving stock to storage is not unusual before a storm, is it?", "\"It is not unusual. Here, there was no storm warning that week, and the stock moved was the newest and most valuable.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned the showroom after moving the stock.", "A tenant whose heater failed."),
        allocution: "\"I hurt someone who didn't deserve it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} moved the best pieces and left the damaged stock.", "{DL} had raised the insurance policy a month earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you set fire to the showroom?", "\"No. I did not. That showroom was my business and my livelihood. I would not destroy it, and I have been devastated by the loss.\""), .direct("Why did you move stock to a storage unit the week before?", "\"I was afraid of a flood. We had an earlier water problem, and a storm was in the forecast. I wanted the best pieces safe.\""), .direct("Why did you leave the damaged stock behind?", "\"It was not worth the trouble of moving. I took the pieces I could sell for the most, and I left the ones that were already scratched.\""), .direct("Why did you disarm the cameras that night?", "\"I stopped by to check on the building and turned off the system so it would not alarm. I left, and I did not go back that night.\""), .direct("What do you think started the fire?", "\"I think the space heater. I had it plugged into a power strip because the back room was cold, and I should have unplugged it.\""), .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"I lost everything I had built. I felt sick, and I knew people would think I did it, and I do not know how to change that.\""), .cross("You cannot explain two points of origin, can you?", "\"No. I do not know how there could be two. I am not an investigator, and I can only tell you I did not do it.\""), .cross("You raised the insurance a month before the fire, didn't you?", "\"Yes. My agent suggested it because of inventory growth. I did not raise it for any other reason.\""), .cross("You moved the best stock and left the worst, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It looks bad, but I was worried about the flood and took what mattered most to my income.\""), .cross("You disarmed the cameras at 11:48 p.m., just before the fire, didn't you?", "\"I did. I know how that looks. I was there for a few minutes, and I left. I did not set anything.\""), .cross("An accelerant was found on the floor at both origins, wasn't it?", "\"That is what the marshal says. Nothing like that was ever stored in the showroom. I did not bring anything flammable into the showroom.\"")],
        openings: ("A furniture showroom burned at night after the tenant moved the newest stock to storage, disarmed the cameras with a personal code, and raised the insurance a month earlier.", "{D} lost a business to a fire that started from a space heater. Moving stock before a flood warning is a precaution, not a plan to burn a building."),
        closings: ("Two points of origin, an accelerant on the floor, the alarm disarmed at 11:48 p.m., and the best stock in storage. These facts fit only one explanation.", "The marshal admits a space heater was plugged in near an origin, and the flood fear was real. Nobody saw {D} set a fire."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The insurance policy is raised."), (-7, "The stock is moved."), (0, "11:48 p.m.: the cameras are disarmed."), (0, "12:30 a.m.: the fire."), (1, "The marshal's findings.")],
        identified: "A fire marshal's report.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let fireDeptFundsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fireDeptFunds",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Treasurer of Volunteer Fire Company Short $63,000 After Nine Years", "New Chief Finds Empty Account While Buying Turnout Gear"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "As treasurer of a volunteer fire department, a nonprofit corporation, fraudulently embezzled over $60,000 entrusted to {D.him}, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 42...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} kept the books for a volunteer fire department for nine years, signing checks and depositing fish fry, raffle and county money. When the new chief tried to buy a $12,000 set of turnout gear, the account held far less than {D}'s reports said. An audit found $63,000 moved to {D}'s accounts. {DL} says {D.he} advanced personal money for the department and was repaying {D.himself}.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Audit", "$63,000 moved to {D}'s accounts."), E(.document, 3, "Altered Reports", "Treasurer reports showed false balances."), E(.document, 3, "Check Register", "Checks written to {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Personal Advances", "{DL} says {D.he} fronted money and repaid {D.himself}.")],
        role: "Forensic accountant",
        exam: [.direct("What did your audit of the fire department's books reveal?", "\"$63,000 had been moved from the department's accounts into accounts held by {D}. The transfers and checks spanned nine years, with larger amounts in the later years.\""), .direct("How did the audit begin?", "\"The new chief tried to buy a $12,000 set of turnout gear and found the account held far less than the treasurer's reports said. The county asked for an audit.\""), .direct("What did the treasurer's reports show compared with the bank statements?", "\"The reports showed balances that were higher than the bank statements. The numbers were altered by hand, and the changes were consistent over three years.\""), .direct("How was money handled at the department?", "\"Fish fry, raffle and county funds were deposited by {DL}. {DL} signed the checks, and no second signature was required by the department.\""), .direct("What did the check register show?", "\"Checks written to {D.him} in round amounts, many with no description. Some were made to cash, and there were no matching invoices or receipts.\""), .direct("Was there any record of the advances {D} says were made to the department?", "\"No. There was no loan agreement, no receipts for purchases, and no entry in the books showing money going in from {D.him}.\""), .cross("The department had no policy requiring two signatures, did it?", "\"No. That was a weakness in the controls. {D.He} had sole authority over the books for nine years.\""), .cross("Volunteer departments often run informally, don't they?", "\"They do. Informality is common. That is why proper records are important, and that is why we found the gaps.\""), .cross("{D} did buy some things for the department, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Possibly. Some equipment purchases were made. I cannot match them to any claim of repayment without receipts.\""), .cross("No one on the board asked to see the bank statements, did they?", "\"I understand not. The board relied on {D.his} reports. That is a failing, but it does not change what the statements show.\""), .cross("You cannot say what {D} was thinking when the checks were written, can you?", "\"No. I can say what the books and statements show. I do not know what {D.he} thought.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took the department's money.", "A volunteer repaying {D.himself}."),
        allocution: "\"I knew better. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no receipts for any advances.", "{DL} altered reports for three years."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the money from the fire department's accounts?", "\"I paid myself back. Over the years I paid for supplies and repairs from my own pocket, and I took the money back when the account allowed.\""), .direct("What kinds of things did you pay for?", "\"Hoses, tools, a small generator, and food for events. I always meant to write it down, and most of it never made it into the books.\""), .direct("Why do you have no receipts?", "\"I kept them in a box in my garage, and the box was lost in a move. I know that makes it hard to prove, and I regret it.\""), .direct("Why did you alter the treasurer's reports?", "\"I made mistakes and tried to correct them by hand. I did not want the board to see sloppy numbers, and I should have asked for help.\""), .direct("Did the board approve your repayments?", "\"Informally. At a few meetings I mentioned that I was getting back what I had advanced, and no one objected.\""), .direct("How do you feel about the audit?", "\"Ashamed. I gave nine years to the department, and I let the records fall apart. I never meant to hurt the department.\""), .cross("No board vote ever approved paying you back, did it?", "\"No formal vote. I mentioned it in meetings, and I understand a mention is not an approval.\""), .cross("You altered reports for three years, didn't you?", "\"I changed numbers by hand. I called them corrections, but I know they made the balances look better than they were.\""), .cross("You signed checks to yourself without a second signature, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was how we did it. I should have insisted on a second signature, and I did not.\""), .cross("The account could not cover a $12,000 set of gear, could it?", "\"No. When the chief tried to buy the gear, the money was not there, and I am sorry for that.\""), .cross("$63,000 is a lot to repay in nine years, isn't it?", "\"It is a lot. I do not think I advanced that much, and I cannot prove what I did.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} kept the books for a volunteer fire department for nine years. When the new chief tried to buy $12,000 in turnout gear, the account held far less than the reports said.", "{D} fronted personal money for hoses, tools and supplies, and took it back over the years. The records are a mess, but a mess is not a theft."),
        closings: ("An audit found $63,000 moved to {D}'s accounts, reports altered for three years, and checks signed to {D} with no loan, no receipt, and no vote.", "{D} gave nine years to a volunteer department and paid for things out of pocket. A missing receipt box is poor bookkeeping, not a crime."),
        timeline: [(-3285, "Treasurer begins."), (-365, "Checks to {D} begin."), (0, "The chief checks the account."), (30, "The audit.")],
        identified: "An audit.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"])

    static let restaurantTipSkimV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.restaurantTipSkim",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Hotel Valet Accused of Pocketing Shared Tip Box Cash Over Several Weeks", "Hidden Camera at the Valet Stand Shows Hands in the Box"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole $380 in shared tips belonging to {V}, a hotel's valet staff, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Hotel valets pool their cash tips in a locked box at the stand and split them at the end of the week. After a run of short splits, the valet supervisor, {V}, put a camera over the box. On {DATE} the camera showed {D}, a valet, unlock the box with a spare key and slide bills into a jacket pocket on two different shifts. {DL} says the cash was {D.his} own tips, put in the box by mistake.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Stand Camera", "{D} unlocks the box and pockets bills."), E(.document, 2, "Tip Log", "Weekly totals $380 below the usual."), E(.physical, 2, "Spare Key", "A key matching the box found in {D}'s locker.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Own Tips", "{DL} says the bills were {D.his} own tips."), E(.statement, 1, "Mistake", "{DL} says {D.he} put them in the wrong place.")],
        role: "Valet supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("How do the hotel valets handle their tips?", "\"Every valet puts cash tips into a locked box at the stand. At the end of each week we count the box and split it evenly among the valets who worked.\""), .direct("Why did you put a camera over the tip box?", "\"Several weeks in a row the splits came up short. I could not see how the box could be short without someone taking from it, so I installed a camera.\""), .direct("What did the camera show on {DATE}?", "\"{D} unlocked the box with a key, slid several bills into a jacket pocket, and locked it again. The same thing happened on a second shift.\""), .direct("How much was missing in the weekly totals?", "\"About $380 below the usual average over the week the camera covered. The numbers had been dropping for several weeks before that.\""), .direct("Where was the spare key found?", "\"In {D.his} locker, during a search with the hotel's security. It matched the lock on the tip box and was not one of the keys we issued.\""), .direct("Who is supposed to have keys to the box?", "\"Only me and the cashier. There are two keys, and both are accounted for. The third key found in the locker was not on the list.\""), .cross("The cashier also has a key, doesn't the cashier?", "\"Yes. The cashier has one, and I have the other. Both keys were with us on the shifts in question.\""), .cross("The camera does not show how many bills {D} took, does it?", "\"No. The angle shows the hand going into the box and into the pocket, but it does not show a count.\""), .cross("Some valets keep their own tip cash on them, don't they?", "\"Yes. People carry their own money. But it is not supposed to go into the shared box and then come out again.\""), .cross("{D} told you the bills were {D.his} own tips, didn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D.he} said afterward. I did not see anyone count the bills in the box before or after.\""), .cross("You cannot say the splits were short because of {D} alone, can you?", "\"I can say the camera shows {DL} taking bills on two shifts. I cannot say what happened on other weeks without footage.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took from the shared tip box.", "A valet who took back {D.his} own tips."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was the only valet short of cash all month.", "{DL} bought a used scooter for $380 the next day."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take bills from the tip box?", "\"I took bills, yes, but I believed they were my own tips. I had put them in the wrong place by mistake, and I took them back.\""), .direct("How did your own tips end up in the shared box?", "\"I was getting a lot of tips in my pocket that night, and I dropped some in the box with the pooled cash. I realized later it was a mix-up.\""), .direct("Why did you have a key to the box?", "\"I borrowed a spare from a coworker to get something out of the box. I meant to return it, and I forgot it in my locker.\""), .direct("Why did you not tell the supervisor what had happened?", "\"I meant to. I was embarrassed that I had made a mistake, and I did not want to explain it in front of everyone.\""), .direct("How much did you take out of the box?", "\"A few bills each time. I did not count it carefully. I only took what I thought was mine, and I did not think it was a large amount.\""), .direct("How did it feel when the supervisor confronted you?", "\"Awful. I was scared and defensive, and I said things I should not have. I should have just explained and apologized.\""), .cross("You bought a used scooter for $380 the next day, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I had been saving for it for a while. It was a coincidence, and I understand why it looks the way it does.\""), .cross("You were the only valet short of cash that month, weren't you?", "\"I was short. I do not know about the others. I had car payments and a lot of bills, and money was tight.\""), .cross("You took money on two different shifts, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It happened twice. I thought each time that I was taking back what was mine.\""), .cross("A spare key in your locker is not an accident, is it?", "\"I borrowed it, and I should have returned it. I did not think about it again until security asked.\""), .cross("You could have asked the supervisor to open the box, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have. I did not want to make a fuss, and I took the easy way.\"")],
        openings: ("Hotel valets pool their tips in a locked box. After weeks of short splits, a camera showed {D} unlock the box with a spare key and slide bills into a jacket pocket on two shifts.", "{D} put some personal tips in the wrong place and took them back. That was a mistake about the box and not a plan to steal from coworkers."),
        closings: ("A camera, a spare key found in {D}'s locker, a $380 shortfall, and a scooter bought the next day. {D} took tips that belonged to the whole team.", "No one counted the bills and no one can say they were not {D}'s own. A mix-up at a tip box is a mistake, not a theft."),
        timeline: [(-21, "The splits start to run short."), (-7, "{V} installs the camera."), (0, "The camera records {D}."), (0, "{V} reviews the footage."), (1, "{V} reports it.")],
        identified: "A stand camera.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .female])

    static let kennelFireAnimalsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.kennelFireAnimals",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Boarding Kennel Fire Kills Eleven Dogs; Owner's Debts and Insurance Raise Questions", "Fire Marshal Finds Accelerant Near Front Office"],
        law: "burningBuildings",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Willfully and maliciously burned a building owned by {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A boarding kennel burned before dawn on {DATE}, killing eleven dogs. The fire marshal found accelerant near the front office. {V} owned the building and leased it to {D}, who ran the kennel and had fallen behind on rent and loans. {DL} says an electrical fault started the fire.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Fire Marshal Report", "Accelerant near the front office."), E(.document, 3, "Rent Ledger", "Four months behind."), E(.document, 2, "Loan Notices", "Two default notices to {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Electrical Fault", "{DL} says the wiring was old.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("Where did the fire start at the kennel?", "\"Near the front office, in the area just inside the entrance. That is where the burn patterns were deepest and where the fire spread out along the corridor.\""), .direct("What evidence of an accelerant did you find?", "\"The lab found an ignitable liquid residue in the debris near the office floor. The pattern on the floor matched a liquid poured and ignited.\""), .direct("How many animals were lost in the fire?", "\"Eleven dogs. They were boarding that night. Staff had gone home, and nobody was inside when the fire started.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s finances?", "\"{D} was four months behind on rent and had received two default notices on loans. The kennel was struggling financially.\""), .direct("Who owned the building?", "\"{V}. {V} leased it to {DL}, who ran the kennel. The lease required rent on the first of each month, and {V} had sent notices of the arrears.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the records that were kept at the kennel?", "\"{DL} had removed the business records from the office the day before the fire. They were later found at {DL}'s home.\""), .cross("The wiring in the building was old, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was older than current code and had some worn insulation. We examined it closely and found no sign of an electrical fault at the origin.\""), .cross("You did not find a short circuit at the point of origin, did you?", "\"No. We examined the panel and the wires near the office. The arcing we found was farther down the line and was a result of the fire.\""), .cross("Many businesses have debts, don't they?", "\"Most do. Debts alone prove nothing. They matter here because they come with the accelerant and the removed records.\""), .cross("You cannot say who poured the liquid, can you?", "\"No. I can say where and how it was started. I cannot say who was there.\""), .cross("{D} was cooperative after the fire, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} answered questions and gave a statement. {D.he} was upset about the dogs, and I would not say {D.he} was uncooperative.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} burned a kennel full of dogs.", "Old wiring."),
        allocution: "\"I hurt someone who didn't deserve it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was the last person to leave.", "{DL} had removed {D.his} own records the day before."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you set fire to the kennel?", "\"No. I would never do that. Those dogs were in my care. I lost my business and I lost eleven animals I cared about.\""), .direct("Why were you the last person to leave that night?", "\"I always close up. I check every run, feed the late dogs, and lock the front door. I left around ten and did not go back.\""), .direct("Why did you take the records home the day before?", "\"I was working on my taxes and a loan application. I took them home to finish the paperwork. It had nothing to do with the fire.\""), .direct("What do you think caused the fire?", "\"The wiring. The building was old, and a few outlets sparked from time to time. I told the owner, and nothing was done.\""), .direct("What was your financial situation?", "\"I was behind on rent, and I had loan payments I could not meet. I was working on a plan and had talked to the bank.\""), .direct("How do you feel about losing the dogs?", "\"I cry about it. I knew every one of them by name. Some had been with me for years, and the owners were counting on me.\""), .cross("You were four months behind on rent, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was behind, and I was working on a payment plan. Many small businesses fall behind from time to time.\""), .cross("You took the records home the day before the fire, didn't you?", "\"I did, because I was doing paperwork. I know the timing looks bad, and I did not plan it.\""), .cross("You were the last person at the kennel, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I always am. That does not mean I set a fire, and I would never hurt those dogs.\""), .cross("You did not report the old wiring in writing, did you?", "\"I told the owner by phone, and I should have put it in writing, and that was an oversight.\""), .cross("Insurance would pay for the loss, wouldn't it?", "\"I believe there was a policy. It would not bring back the dogs, and I would never have done it for money.\"")],
        openings: ("A boarding kennel burned before dawn and eleven dogs died. The fire marshal found accelerant near the front office, and the tenant was months behind on rent and loans.", "{D} loved the animals in the kennel and lost everything in the fire. The building was old, and old wiring is a more likely cause than a person."),
        closings: ("Accelerant near the office, four months of unpaid rent, two default notices, and records removed the day before. The fire was set.", "The marshal found old wiring and no one who saw {D} set a fire. {D} lost eleven dogs and a business and had no reason to destroy them."),
        timeline: [(-120, "Rent falls behind."), (-1, "Records are removed."), (0, "The fire."), (1, "The marshal's findings.")],
        identified: "A fire marshal's report.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let weddingRingPawnV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.weddingRingPawn",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Caregiver Pawned Widow's Wedding Ring and Heirloom Brooch for $400", "Pawn Tickets in Aide's Name Lead Daughter to Police"],
        law: "exploitationElder",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Obtained property of {V}, an older adult, valued at $5,800 by deception while in a position of trust, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...34,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, 84, widowed, noticed a wedding ring and a family brooch missing. A relative found pawn tickets for both in the name of {D}, a home aide. The items were pawned for $400 and valued at $5,800. {DL} says {V} gave them to {D.him} as a gift.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Pawn Tickets", "Both items pawned by {D}."), E(.document, 2, "Appraisal", "$5,800 for both items."), E(.statement, 2, "Relative", "{V} never gave anything away.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Gift", "{DL} says {V} gave them freely.")],
        role: "Adult protective services worker",
        exam: [.direct("What did {V} tell you about the wedding ring and brooch?", "\"That they were not gifts. {V} said they were keepsakes from a late spouse and family, and that {V} would never have given them away.\""), .direct("How were the missing items discovered?", "\"A relative noticed the ring and brooch were not in {V}'s jewelry box. The relative then found two pawn tickets in the name of {D}.\""), .direct("What were the pawn tickets for?", "\"Both items, pawned for $400 together. An appraisal later valued the ring and brooch at $5,800, far more than the pawn loan.\""), .direct("What is {V}'s situation?", "\"{V} is 84, widowed, and lives alone with help from a home aide. {V} depends on that help for meals, bathing and light housework.\""), .direct("How did {V} react when you asked about the items?", "\"{V} was upset and tearful, and repeated that they were not gifts. {V} was clear on that point even when other things were hazy.\""), .direct("What did you learn about when the items were pawned?", "\"Within a week of {DL} noticing them. The family was never told, and {V} was not consulted about any sale or loan.\""), .cross("{V} is sometimes confused, isn't {V}?", "\"At times. {V} has bad days, and some days {V} is very clear. I believed {V} on this point, and I wrote that down.\""), .cross("{V} did give {D} small things on earlier occasions, didn't {V}?", "\"I understand there were small gifts, like candy and a scarf. Nothing of this value was ever given before.\""), .cross("No written note records a gift of the ring, does it?", "\"There is no written note either way. That is common with older adults, and it is why the circumstances matter.\""), .cross("{D} was a good aide in other respects, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"I have heard good things about {D.his} care. That does not change what the pawn tickets show.\""), .cross("You did not see {V} hand anything to {D}, did you?", "\"No. I was not there. I rely on what {V} told me, what the relative found, and the pawn records.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} pawned an older adult's keepsakes.", "A gift."),
        allocution: "\"I took advantage of someone who trusted me, and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} pawned them within a week.", "{DL} gave no word to the family."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did {V} give you the ring and the brooch?", "\"Yes. {V} said I had been so kind and wanted me to have something. {V} put them in my hand and said they were mine.\""), .direct("Why did you pawn them?", "\"I needed money for rent. I told myself I could get them back later. I took a $400 loan, and I did not think about their real value.\""), .direct("Why did you not tell the family?", "\"I was embarrassed. I knew it would sound bad. I wanted to redeem the items before anyone noticed, and I ran out of time.\""), .direct("What was your relationship with {V}?", "\"I was {V}'s aide for about a year. We got along well and talked every day. {V} often said I was like family.\""), .direct("What do you want {V} to know?", "\"That I am sorry I hurt {V}'s trust. I should have kept the gift or returned it, and not pawned it.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned the family was upset?", "\"I offered to get the items back. I told them where the pawn shop was and gave them the tickets.\""), .cross("You pawned both items within a week, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was behind on rent and I made a rushed decision. I know it looks bad.\""), .cross("You did not tell {V}'s family about the gift, did you?", "\"No, I did not. I should have, and I was embarrassed.\""), .cross("A gift of a wedding ring is a serious thing, isn't it?", "\"It is. {V} insisted, and I accepted it. I should have asked the family before I took something so valuable.\""), .cross("You took $400 for items worth $5,800, didn't you?", "\"I did. I did not know the value. I only knew I needed rent money, and I did not have the items appraised.\""), .cross("{V} says it was not a gift, doesn't {V}?", "\"That is what {V} says now. I remember it differently, and I cannot prove it either way.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, 84 and widowed, noticed a wedding ring and a family brooch were missing. Pawn tickets for both were in the name of {D}, a home aide, and they were worth $5,800.", "{D} cared for {V} for a year and was given the ring as a gift. Pawning it was unwise, but a gift is not a theft."),
        closings: ("{V} says the items were never given, a relative found the tickets, and {D} pawned them within a week for $400. That is taking advantage of someone who trusted {D}.", "{V} often told {D} that {D.he} was like family. A gift that is later regretted is not a crime, and {D} offered to return the items."),
        timeline: [(-14, "{D} starts work."), (-7, "The items vanish."), (0, "A relative finds the tickets."), (3, "A report is filed.")],
        identified: "Pawn tickets.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "mistakeOfFact"],
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let pistolFromTruckV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pistolFromTruck",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Unlocked Truck in Driveway Emptied of Handgun and Tools", "Stolen Pistol Turns Up in a Traffic Stop"],
        law: "larcenyFirearm",
