        spec: "Stole a firearm belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 19...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A pistol, a nail gun and a toolbox were taken from {V}'s unlocked truck on {DATE}. Two weeks later, {D} was stopped for a headlight and the pistol was under the seat. {DL} says {D.he} bought it from a vendor at a flea market.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Pistol", "Serial number matches the theft report."), E(.document, 3, "Traffic Stop Report", "Under {D}'s seat."), E(.physical, 1, "Toolbox", "Not recovered.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Flea Market", "{DL} says {D.he} bought it at a flea market.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Where was the pistol found when you stopped {D}?", "\"Under the driver's seat, within reach. I saw it during a stop for a broken headlight, after {D} gave consent for me to look inside.\""), .direct("Whose pistol was it?", "\"{V}'s. The serial number matched a theft report filed two weeks earlier, after the pistol, a nail gun and a toolbox were taken from an unlocked truck.\""), .direct("What else was taken from {V}'s truck?", "\"A nail gun and a toolbox. Neither has been recovered. The truck was unlocked, and nothing was damaged in the theft.\""), .direct("What did the defendant tell you about the pistol?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} bought it from a vendor at a flea market for cash. {D.he} did not have a receipt and could not name the vendor.\""), .direct("What did you do after you found it?", "\"I checked the serial number against the stolen property list and found a match. I took the pistol into evidence and arrested {D.him}.\""), .direct("What condition was the pistol in?", "\"It was clean and loaded. There was a full magazine in it and one round in the chamber, and it had been recently handled.\""), .cross("{D} was cooperative during the stop, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} pulled over, handed me the documents, and answered questions. {D.he} did not try to hide the pistol.\""), .cross("Flea markets do sell used pistols sometimes, don't they?", "\"Some do, though private sales still require care. I cannot say whether a vendor at a flea market sold this one.\""), .cross("You cannot say who took the pistol from {V}'s truck, can you?", "\"No. I can only say that it was in {DL}'s car two weeks later. I do not know who took it.\""), .cross("The toolbox and nail gun were not found with the defendant, were they?", "\"No. Neither was found with {D.him}, and nothing from the truck besides the pistol turned up in the stop.\""), .cross("{D} had no prior history with stolen firearms, did {D.he}?", "\"Not that I found. {D.He} had a clean record on that point, and I made a note of it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} had a stolen pistol.", "A bargain at a flea market."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} knew the pistol was cheap.", "{DL} could not name the seller."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the pistol from {V}'s truck?", "\"No. I never saw {V}'s truck. I bought the pistol from a vendor at a flea market a few days before I was stopped.\""), .direct("Why did you buy a pistol at a flea market?", "\"I wanted something for protection at home. A vendor had a table with a few pistols, and the price was good, so I bought one.\""), .direct("What do you remember about the seller?", "\"A person at a small folding table with several items, who took cash and did not give a name. I never got a card or a receipt.\""), .direct("Why did you keep the pistol under the seat?", "\"I was driving it home from a friend's place after buying it. I put it under the seat for the drive and never moved it.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy stopped you?", "\"I handed over my license and told the deputy about the pistol right away. I did not hide it, and I cooperated.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I would not buy something like that without a bill of sale. I know now that a cheap price and no paper should have told me something.\""), .cross("The pistol was cheap, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was priced well below what I expected. I thought I had found a bargain, and I did not ask why.\""), .cross("You cannot name the seller, can you?", "\"No. I wish I could. I did not ask for a name or write down anything about the table.\""), .cross("You paid cash and got no receipt, didn't you?", "\"That is right. It was cash and a handshake, and I did not think about proof.\""), .cross("A pistol with a serial number that matches a theft report was in your car, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, I understand that. Nothing told me it was stolen. I only learned that when the deputy ran the number.\""), .cross("You knew buying a pistol with no paperwork was risky, didn't you?", "\"I did not think about the risk as I should have. I wanted a pistol and a good price, and I paid for that mistake.\"")],
        openings: ("A pistol, a nail gun and a toolbox were taken from {V}'s unlocked truck. Two weeks later, a deputy found the pistol under {D}'s seat, and its serial number matched the theft report.", "{D} bought a pistol from a flea market vendor and kept it under the seat in plain view of a deputy. {D} did not know it was stolen."),
        closings: ("The serial number matches {V}'s stolen pistol, and the pistol was under {D}'s seat two weeks after the theft. {D} has no receipt, no paper, and cannot name the seller.", "{D} was honest with the deputy and told the story right away without hiding the pistol. A bargain with no paper is a mistake, not a theft."),
        timeline: [(0, "The theft."), (1, "{V} reports."), (14, "The traffic stop."), (15, "The serial number is run.")],
        identified: "A serial number.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let dogsKillChildV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.dogsKillChild",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Toddler Dies in Yard After Two Dogs Break Through Rotted Gate", "Owner Warned Twice About the Fence"],
