        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unintentionally killed {V} while committing a culpable negligence by failing to secure two dangerous dogs, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a toddler, wandered through an open gate into {D}'s neighbor yard on {DATE}, and two dogs attacked and killed {V.him}. The gate had a rotted latch. Animal control had warned {D} twice about the dogs and the fence. {DL} says {D.he} meant to fix the latch that week.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Animal Control Warnings", "Two written warnings about the fence."), E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Examiner", "Fatal injuries from the dogs."), E(.physical, 2, "Gate Latch", "Rotted through.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Fix Planned", "{DL} says {D.he} had bought the part.")],
        role: "Animal control officer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you arrived at the scene on {DATE}?", "\"A toddler who had died of injuries from two dogs, and two dogs still in the yard behind a gate. The gate stood open and hung from one hinge.\""), .direct("What did you find when you examined the gate latch?", "\"The latch was rotted through. The wood around it was soft and crumbled in my fingers, and it could not have held the gate closed against a push.\""), .direct("What warnings had animal control given {D} before this?", "\"Two written warnings. The first was about the dogs running loose, and the second was about the fence and the gate and their condition.\""), .direct("What did the warnings tell the defendant to do?", "\"To repair the fence and the gate and keep the dogs secured. Each notice gave a deadline, and the second said further action might follow.\""), .direct("What did the medical examiner conclude?", "\"That the injuries were fatal and were caused by the dogs. The examiner's report describes injuries consistent with an attack by two large dogs.\""), .direct("Where were the dogs usually kept?", "\"Outside in the yard, day and night. Neighbors told us they were never brought indoors, even in bad weather.\""), .cross("{D} did buy a replacement part for the latch, didn't {D.he}?", "\"A receipt was found for a latch part bought a few days before. The part was still in its package in the garage.\""), .cross("The gate was not meant to be open that day, was it?", "\"No. It should have been closed. But the latch had rotted and the gate had swung open on its own.\""), .cross("The dogs had not attacked anyone else before, had they?", "\"One dog had bitten {D} earlier. There was no report of a bite to a neighbor, and I cannot say more about their history.\""), .cross("{D} was devastated when you told {D.him} what had happened, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} was in tears and could not speak. It was a difficult scene, and I would not say {D.he} was indifferent.\""), .cross("The toddler walked into the yard on {V.his} own, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Yes, {V.he} wandered through the open gate. That is why a secure latch matters so much with children in the neighborhood.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ignored two warnings and a child died.", "A tragic accident."),
        allocution: "\"I should have walked away.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been bitten before by one of the dogs.", "The dogs were never kept inside."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you receive warnings from animal control about the fence?", "\"Yes, twice. The officer told me to fix the fence and the gate, and I said I would. I meant to, and I put it off.\""), .direct("What did you do after the second warning?", "\"I bought a replacement latch. It sat in my garage for a few days, and I planned to install it that week, before it happened.\""), .direct("Why had you not fixed the latch sooner?", "\"I was working long hours and I kept telling myself there would be time on the weekend. I wish more than anything I had done it that same day.\""), .direct("Where did the dogs stay?", "\"In the yard. They liked being outside and I had a fence, and I thought the fence was good enough. I was wrong.\""), .direct("Had either dog ever hurt anyone before?", "\"One of them had bitten me once, in the hand, when I broke up a fight. I did not think of the dogs as dangerous to others.\""), .direct("What do you want {V}'s family to know?", "\"That I am so sorry. {V} is in my thoughts all the time. No apology will ever be enough, and I will never forgive myself.\""), .cross("You were warned twice and did not fix the gate, did you?", "\"That is true. I did not fix it, and I have to live with that. I take responsibility for it.\""), .cross("One of your dogs had bitten you before, hadn't it?", "\"Yes. I should have taken that more seriously. I thought it was a one-time thing during a fight.\""), .cross("You kept the dogs outside, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I never brought them in, and I should have kept them inside or in a pen with a secure lock.\""), .cross("The part you bought was still in the package, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, it was. I never got to it. I will always wish I had put it in the day I bought it.\""), .cross("You knew a latch that is rotted can open on its own, didn't you?", "\"I knew it was weak. I did not think the gate would swing open. I should have chained it shut at the least.\"")],
        openings: ("A toddler wandered through an open gate with a rotted latch and was killed by two dogs. Animal control had warned {D} twice about the dogs and the fence.", "{D} bought the part to fix the latch and meant to install it that week. This was a tragic accident, and {D} grieves for {V}."),
        closings: ("Two written warnings, a rotted latch, and a part that stayed in the garage. A child died because the gate was not fixed.", "{D} bought the part, planned the repair, and is heartbroken over what happened to {V}. A tragedy and a mistake are not the same as a crime."),
        timeline: [(-60, "First warning."), (-14, "Second warning."), (0, "The attack."), (1, "The examiner.")],
        identified: "Written warnings.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .female])

    static let fakeFundraiserV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fakeFundraiser",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Online Fundraiser for 'Sick Child' Raised $24,000 for Someone Who Wasn't Sick", "Hospital Says No Such Patient"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "By means of a false pretense, obtained $24,000 from {V}, a donor, intending to cheat and defraud, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 28...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} posted a fundraiser for a child said to have cancer. It raised $24,000 from hundreds of donors, including {V}. A hospital said it had no such patient. The money went to {D}'s accounts. {DL} says {D.he} meant to pass the money on to a family.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Fundraiser Page", "{D} as organizer with photos of a child."), E(.document, 3, "Hospital Letter", "No patient by that name."), E(.document, 3, "Bank Records", "Funds moved to {D}'s accounts.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Family", "{DL} says a family would receive it.")],
        role: "Fraud investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did the fundraiser page claim?", "\"That a child had cancer and the family needed help with medical bills. {D} appeared as the organizer, with photos of a child and an emotional story.\""), .direct("How much did the fundraiser raise, and from how many donors?", "\"$24,000 from hundreds of donors. {V} was one of them. Most gave between $20 and $100, in response to shared posts on social media.\""), .direct("What did you learn when you contacted the hospital named on the page?", "\"The hospital said it had no patient by that name and no record of any such treatment. A spokesperson confirmed that in writing.\""), .direct("Where did the donations go?", "\"Into accounts held by {DL}. The bank records show the money moved in within days of each donation, and none of it went to a medical provider.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the photos on the page?", "\"They were stock photos found on several unrelated sites. The child in the photos is not connected to {D.him} or to any known patient.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about the family?", "\"That the money was meant to go to a family {DL} knew. {DL} offered a name late in the interview, but we could not find any such family.\""), .cross("Many donors give without checking the details, don't they?", "\"Yes, that is the nature of online giving. Donors trust the page. That is why it is a serious matter when the page is false.\""), .cross("{D} did return some money to donors, didn't {D.he}?", "\"I understand some small refunds were issued after the page was reported. They were a small fraction of the total.\""), .cross("The photos might have been used with a real family's consent, mightn't they?", "\"They were stock photos from the internet. I found no consent or connection to a family, and none was offered.\""), .cross("{D} cooperated with your investigation, didn't {D.he}?", "\"{D.He} agreed to talk and handed over some records. I would not say {D.he} refused anything.\""), .cross("You cannot say what the defendant intended when the page was created, can you?", "\"No. I can say what the page said, what the hospital said, and where the money went. Intent is for the jury.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} invented a sick child to raise money.", "A fundraiser meant for a family."),
        allocution: "\"It was wrong from the start, and I knew it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} used the money on a vacation.", "The family does not exist."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you create the fundraiser page for a child with cancer?", "\"I created the page. I believed the story at first. A friend told me about a sick child, and I wanted to help.\""), .direct("Who told you about the child?", "\"A friend of a friend. I never met the family, and I took the story on faith. I should have verified it before I posted.\""), .direct("Why did the money go into your accounts?", "\"I did not have another account set up. I planned to send it to the family once I found them, and I put it where I could access it.\""), .direct("What did you spend the money on?", "\"Some went toward a trip, which I treated as a loan to myself. I told myself I would pay it back before the family needed anything.\""), .direct("Why did you use photos from the internet?", "\"I did not have photos from the family, so I used pictures I found. I thought it would help the page reach more people.\""), .direct("What do you want donors to know?", "\"That I am sorry. I let them down and I let myself down. I should never have taken the money, and I want to make it right.\""), .cross("There is no family, is there?", "\"I cannot find one. I thought the story was real, and I understand now that it was not.\""), .cross("You spent donor money on a vacation, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I called it a loan in my head. It was wrong, and I know I should not have touched it.\""), .cross("You used stock photos of a child to ask strangers for money, didn't you?", "\"I did. I did not think about how that would look. It was wrong to present a stranger's picture as the sick child.\""), .cross("The hospital had no record of any patient, did it?", "\"That is what I learned later. I never called the hospital, and I should have checked before I posted.\""), .cross("You gave the investigator a family name only late in the interview, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was scared and grasping for something. It did not help, and I should have been honest from the start.\"")],
        openings: ("A fundraiser for a child with cancer raised $24,000 from hundreds of donors. The hospital had no such patient, the photos were stock images, and the money went to {D}'s accounts.", "{D} meant to help a family and was taken in by a story that was not true. A good intention that went wrong is not the same as fraud."),
        closings: ("No patient, no family, stock photos, and $24,000 in {D}'s accounts. Hundreds of people gave to a child who does not exist.", "{D} believed the story and set out to help. Spending the money was wrong, but {D} did not invent a sick child."),
        timeline: [(-45, "The page goes up."), (-10, "The goal is met."), (0, "The hospital replies."), (5, "A tip reaches police.")],
        identified: "A fundraiser page.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let atvTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.atvTheft",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Quad Bike Vanishes From Locked Shed; Paint Job Gives It Away", "Rider in Online Photo Wears a Familiar Jacket"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Stole an all-terrain vehicle valued at $4,800 belonging to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...32,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}'s all-terrain vehicle disappeared from a locked farm shed on {DATE}. Ten days later a deputy followed tire tracks from a field to a barn belonging to a relative of {D}, where the vehicle sat with fresh paint and a swapped plate. {DL} says {D.he} bought it from a coworker and painted it.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "ATV Frame Number", "Stamped number matches {V}'s title."), E(.physical, 3, "Fresh Paint", "Overspray on the barn floor."), E(.document, 2, "Title", "{V} is the registered owner.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Coworker", "{DL} says a coworker sold it for $900.")],
        role: "Sheriff's property crimes detective",
        exam: [.direct("Whose all-terrain vehicle was found in the barn?", "\"{V}'s. It was taken from a locked farm shed. {V} is the registered owner on the title, and the machine is worth about $4,800.\""), .direct("How did you identify the vehicle after it had been repainted?", "\"By the frame number stamped on the frame under the paint. The number matches the number on {V}'s title and registration.\""), .direct("Where did you find the vehicle?", "\"In a barn belonging to a relative of {D}, about ten days after the theft. Tire tracks led from a field to the barn door.\""), .direct("What did you find that showed the vehicle had been altered?", "\"Fresh paint on the body with overspray on the barn floor, and a plate that did not match the vehicle. The original plate was missing.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about how it was obtained?", "\"That {D.he} bought it from a coworker for $900 and painted it. {D.He} did not have a receipt and could not give the coworker's full name.\""), .direct("What did you do to try to confirm the story about a coworker?", "\"I contacted {D.his} employer and checked the staff list. No one matching the description worked there, and no one remembered such a sale.\""), .cross("The vehicle was found in a relative's barn, not the defendant's home, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was in a barn owned by a relative of {DL}. I do not know who had access to it.\""), .cross("Many ATVs are repainted by their owners, aren't they?", "\"It is common to repaint. A paint job alone is not unusual. The overspray and the plate swap, taken together, are what concern me.\""), .cross("The frame number was left in place, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was not ground off. That can be read in more than one way, and I cannot say what {D.he} knew.\""), .cross("No one saw the defendant take the vehicle from the shed, did they?", "\"No. No witness places {DL} at the shed. The shed was locked and the lock was cut.\""), .cross("The coworker could exist even if you did not find one, couldn't they?", "\"It is possible. I could not find any such person, and {DL} could not help me with a name.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} repainted a stolen vehicle.", "A bargain buy from a coworker."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid $900 for a $4,800 machine.", "{DL} swapped the plate."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the all-terrain vehicle?", "\"No. I never went near {V}'s shed. I bought the vehicle from a coworker and I believed it was a legitimate sale.\""), .direct("How did you come to buy it?", "\"A coworker said they needed cash and offered it to me for $900. I looked it over, took it for a ride, and paid in cash.\""), .direct("Why did you paint it?", "\"I like green, and the old color was faded. I painted it myself in a relative's barn. I did not think of it as hiding anything.\""), .direct("Why did you change the plate?", "\"The original was bent and hard to read. I put on another one I had lying around. I did not register the change, and that was a mistake.\""), .direct("Why was it in a relative's barn?", "\"I did not have room at my place. My relative has a barn with extra space and let me keep the vehicle and the paint there.\""), .direct("What did you do when the deputy came?", "\"I explained what I knew and told the deputy about the coworker. I gave the deputy my phone number and offered to help find the seller.\""), .cross("You paid $900 for a machine worth $4,800, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a great price, and I should have wondered why. I did not think hard about it.\""), .cross("You have no receipt, do you?", "\"No. We made a handshake deal. I know that makes me look careless, and I was.\""), .cross("You cannot give the coworker's full name, can you?", "\"I know a first name. I never got a last name or a number I could use, and I should have.\""), .cross("You changed the plate and repainted the vehicle, didn't you?", "\"I did both, within a few days. Taken together I understand it looks like I was hiding something, and I was not.\""), .cross("You kept it in a barn that is not yours, didn't you?", "\"Yes, a relative's barn. I did not try to hide it from anyone, and I told the deputy exactly where it was.\"")],
        openings: ("An all-terrain vehicle vanished from a locked farm shed. Ten days later a deputy found it in a barn with fresh paint, a swapped plate, and a frame number matching {V}'s title.", "{D} bought a vehicle from a coworker, painted it and put it in a relative's barn. {D} did not know it was stolen."),
        closings: ("The frame number matches {V}'s title, the paint was fresh, the plate was swapped, and {D} paid $900 for a $4,800 machine. {D} cannot name the seller.", "{D} paid cash, painted the vehicle, and told the deputy everything. A bargain that was too good to be true is not a theft."),
        timeline: [(0, "The shed is opened."), (1, "{V} reports it."), (10, "The barn."), (11, "The frame number.")],
        identified: "A frame number.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let fleetBrakeWarningV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fleetBrakeWarning",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Quarry Truck Driver Killed on Steep Grade; Maintenance Log Shows Skipped Inspections", "Three Written Warnings Sat in a Drawer"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unintentionally killed {V} without malice through culpable negligence, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a quarry truck driver, died on {DATE} when the brakes failed going downhill. {D}, who ran the equipment yard, had three written warnings from drivers about the brakes and had signed off on the inspection without a road test. {DL} says a mechanic told {D.him} the truck was fine.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Driver Warnings", "Three written brake complaints."), E(.forensic, 3, "Brake Inspection", "Drums worn past limit."), E(.document, 2, "Sign-Off Sheet", "{D} signed without a road test.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Mechanic", "{DL} says the mechanic cleared it.")],
        role: "Safety investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did your investigation find about the brakes on the truck?", "\"The brake drums were worn past the manufacturer's limit and the linings were thin. The brakes could not hold the loaded truck on a steep downhill grade.\""), .direct("What had drivers reported about those brakes?", "\"Three written complaints over the previous weeks, each describing a soft pedal or a long stopping distance. All three were filed with the equipment yard.\""), .direct("Who ran the equipment yard and signed off on the truck?", "\"{D}. {D.He} signed the inspection sheet without a road test, and the truck was returned to service the same day.\""), .direct("What does the company's inspection procedure require?", "\"A visual check and a road test of the brakes before a truck is returned to service after a complaint. The road test line on the form was blank.\""), .direct("How did {V} die?", "\"The brakes failed on a steep downhill haul road. The truck could not slow and went over the edge at a curve. {V} died at the scene.\""), .direct("What did the maintenance shop tell you about its workload?", "\"That it was behind. There was a backlog of trucks, and the shop was working long hours to keep up with demand.\""), .cross("A mechanic told {D} the truck was fine, didn't a mechanic?", "\"{D.He} says so. I interviewed the mechanic, who recalls a brief conversation. There was no written note or report.\""), .cross("The inspection sheet was signed, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The sheet is signed by {DL} and lists the truck as cleared. The road test line was left empty.\""), .cross("The shop was behind on work across the whole fleet, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. That was a company-wide problem. I noted it in my report, and it is a contributing factor.\""), .cross("You cannot say how {V}'s truck was driven that day, can you?", "\"I reviewed the data and interviews. {V} was driving carefully, and I found nothing suggesting a mistake by {V}.\""), .cross("{D} did not intend for anyone to be hurt, did {D.he}?", "\"I have no evidence that {D.he} intended harm. The issue is the decision to sign off without the required test.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ignored warnings and a driver died.", "A mechanic's word."),
        allocution: "\"I let it get out of hand. I'm ashamed.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been told the shop was behind.", "{DL} kept the truck on the road."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you ignore the drivers' warnings about the brakes?", "\"I did not ignore them. I sent the truck to the shop, and the mechanic told me it was fine. I trusted the shop.\""), .direct("Why did you sign the inspection sheet without a road test?", "\"It was routine, and we were short on trucks. I signed because the mechanic had cleared it, and I did not think to insist on a test.\""), .direct("What did the mechanic say to you?", "\"That the brakes were within spec and it could go back on the road. It was a quick conversation in the yard, and nothing was written.\""), .direct("What was the pressure at the yard that month?", "\"We needed every truck on the road. Production was behind, and the shop was swamped. I did not want to pull a truck without a clear reason.\""), .direct("How did you feel when you learned about the accident?", "\"I felt like I had been hit. {V} was a good driver and a friend. I replay the sign-off in my mind every day.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I would have insisted on a road test and kept the truck off the road until it was done. I should have, and I did not.\""), .cross("You signed without a road test, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have waited and insisted on one. I took the mechanic's word, and that was not enough.\""), .cross("Three drivers complained about those brakes, didn't they?", "\"They did. I did not take them seriously enough. I should have pulled the truck until it was fixed.\""), .cross("You kept the truck on the road because you needed it, didn't you?", "\"We needed trucks, yes. That was a factor. I did not put the truck back on the road to hurt anyone.\""), .cross("You were told the shop was behind, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I knew the shop was swamped, and I should have known that meant a quick fix was not enough.\""), .cross("The mechanic's word was not written anywhere, was it?", "\"No. I did not ask for it in writing. I should have, and I will carry that for the rest of my life.\"")],
        openings: ("A quarry truck driver died when the brakes failed going downhill. {D} ran the equipment yard, had three written brake warnings, and signed the inspection without a road test.", "{D} trusted a mechanic who said the truck was fine. {D} made a tragic mistake but never meant to put a driver at risk."),
        closings: ("Three written warnings, worn drums, and an inspection signed without a road test. The truck went back on the road, and {V} died.", "{D} relied on the mechanic and the shop. A verbal clearance from a trusted mechanic is a mistake in judgment, not a crime."),
        timeline: [(-30, "First warning."), (-7, "The sign-off."), (0, "The crash."), (2, "The inspection.")],
        identified: "Written warnings.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let pumpSkimmerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pumpSkimmer",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Gas Station Cameras Capture Technician-Disguised Visitor Opening Pump Panel", "Card Readers Hold Hundreds of Stolen Account Numbers"],
        law: "cardFraud",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Used counterfeit financial transaction cards encoded with account numbers stolen through a skimmer, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 25...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Cardholders began reporting charges in other states after buying gas at one station. A service worker found a hidden skimmer inside a pump. Cameras showed {D} opening the panel with a key twice in two weeks. Cards encoded with the stolen numbers were found in {D}'s car. {DL} says {D.he} was paid to fix the pump and never knew about the device.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Skimmer", "Hidden in the pump panel."), E(.physical, 3, "Counterfeit Cards", "Encoded cards in {D}'s car."), E(.video, 2, "Pump Camera", "{D} opens the panel twice.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Repair Job", "{DL} says a stranger hired {D.him} to fix the pump.")],
        role: "Cardholder",
        exam: [.direct("What happened with your card after you bought gas at that station?", "\"Charges showed up in other states within days, for purchases I never made. I had not left my wallet anywhere, and the only unusual use was that pump.\""), .direct("How did you learn what had happened to your card number?", "\"My bank told me it had been copied and used by a counterfeit card. They said other customers from the same station had the same problem.\""), .direct("What did the service worker find inside the pump?", "\"A hidden skimmer tucked inside the panel, wired to the card reader. It captured card numbers as people paid, and it was placed so no customer could see it.\""), .direct("What did the pump camera show about who had access to the panel?", "\"{D} opened the panel with a key twice in two weeks. Each time it took a few minutes, and {DL} left without speaking to anyone at the station.\""), .direct("What was found in {D}'s car?", "\"Several blank cards encoded with stolen numbers. They were in the glove box, along with a small device for writing data to cards.\""), .direct("How many people were affected?", "\"More than fifty cardholders reported charges, according to the investigators. My bank refunded me, but it took weeks to get new cards.\""), .cross("Gas pumps are serviced by many people, aren't they?", "\"Yes. Technicians and station staff open pump panels regularly. That is why the camera footage is important, to see who was there.\""), .cross("You do not know who installed the skimmer, do you?", "\"No. I know the skimmer was in the pump I used. I was told the camera shows {DL} opening it, but I did not see that myself.\""), .cross("The key the defendant used was a real key, wasn't it?", "\"The investigators said a real key was used, which suggests someone gave it to {DL}, or {DL} had one made.\""), .cross("{D} has a record of doing repair work, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I do not know about {D.his} work history. I only know what the investigators told me about the camera and the cards.\""), .cross("Many people had their cards copied from different places, didn't they?", "\"Cards can be copied in many ways. I know only that mine was used right after I bought gas there.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stole card numbers from a gas pump.", "A repairman used by someone else."),
        allocution: "\"I let money decide it, and I can't take it back.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had the cards in the glove box.", "{DL} said nothing to the owner."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you install the skimmer in the gas pump?", "\"No. I did not know there was a skimmer. I was paid to fix a pump, and I never looked at what was inside beyond the part I was replacing.\""), .direct("Who hired you to fix the pump?", "\"A stranger who said they were from the station owner's company. They gave me a key and cash, and told me which panel to open.\""), .direct("Why did you open the panel twice?", "\"The first time I replaced a card reader part. The second time I was told to check it again because of a complaint. I did not look further.\""), .direct("Where did the cards in your glove box come from?", "\"They were not mine. They were in a bag I was given as part of the job. I did not look at them, and I assumed they were blank supplies.\""), .direct("Why did you not tell the station owner you had opened the panel?", "\"I assumed the owner knew. The stranger said the owner had arranged it, so I did not think I needed to say anything.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies approached you?", "\"I told them everything I knew and gave them the stranger's phone number. I did not know it would turn out to be a number that does not work.\""), .cross("Cards encoded with stolen numbers were in your car, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They were in the glove box. I did not put them there knowing what they were, and I did not realize what they were until later.\""), .cross("You opened the panel twice with a key, didn't you?", "\"Yes. The stranger gave me the key. I should have asked more questions, and I understand how it looks.\""), .cross("You cannot name the stranger, can you?", "\"No. I have a phone number that is no longer in service. I wish I had asked for a name and a card.\""), .cross("You never told the owner about the work, did you?", "\"No. I assumed the owner knew. I now see that I should have checked.\""), .cross("You were paid in cash, weren't you?", "\"Yes. It was cash and I did not get a receipt. That was a mistake, and I should have wondered why.\"")],
        openings: ("Cardholders reported charges in other states after buying gas at one pump. A hidden skimmer was found inside, a camera showed {D} opening the panel twice, and encoded cards were in {D}'s car.", "{D} was paid by a stranger to repair a pump and never knew a skimmer was inside. {D} was used, and did not steal anyone's card numbers."),
        closings: ("The skimmer was in the pump, the camera shows {D} opening it twice, and cards encoded with stolen numbers were in {D}'s glove box. That is no coincidence.", "A stranger gave {D} a key and a job. No one saw {D} install the device, and {D} cooperated from the start."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The first panel opening."), (-1, "The second."), (0, "Charges spike."), (3, "The skimmer is found.")],
        identified: "A pump camera.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "searchSeizure"])

