        summary: "A towing company clamped a wheel immobilizer on {D}'s car for parking in a private lot on {DATE}. {D} returned, cut through the clamp with bolt cutters, and drove off. The clamp was ruined. {DL} says the lot had no signs and the clamp was illegal.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Cut Clamp", "Sheared steel pieces."), E(.video, 3, "Lot Camera", "{D} cuts the clamp."), E(.document, 1, "Replacement Invoice", "$450.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "No Signs", "{DL} says no signs were posted.")],
        role: "Towing company owner",
        exam: [.direct("What does your company do in the private lot?", "\"We manage parking for the lot owner, patrol for unauthorized vehicles, and place immobilizing clamps on cars parked without permission. The owner pays us per lot.\""), .direct("What happened to the clamp on {D}'s car?", "\"It was cut through with bolt cutters. The pieces were left on the ground when {D} drove off, and the clamp could not be repaired.\""), .direct("What does the lot camera show?", "\"It shows {DL} returning to the car with bolt cutters, cutting through the clamp in about a minute, and driving off without speaking to anyone.\""), .direct("What did it cost to replace the clamp?", "\"$450. That is the replacement price for that model, and we invoiced it. The old one was cut in two and was destroyed.\""), .direct("How is a clamp removed when a driver wants the car back?", "\"The driver calls the number on the notice, pays the release fee, and one of our staff comes and takes off the clamp. The fee here is $100.\""), .direct("What notice was placed on the defendant's car?", "\"A bright sticker on the windshield and one on the driver's window. It stated the fee, the number to call, and the lot owner's name.\""), .cross("There were signs posted at the lot, weren't there?", "\"Yes, some. They are by the entrance and along the wall. I understand {DL} says there were none, and I disagree.\""), .cross("The signs are not at every parking space, are they?", "\"No. They are at the entrance and at the far end. A driver parking in the middle might not have walked past one.\""), .cross("The $100 fee is higher than many other lots charge, isn't it?", "\"It may be higher than some. It is set by the lot owner, not by us, and it is posted on the notice.\""), .cross("{D} was told how to get the clamp removed, wasn't {D.he}?", "\"The notice told {D.him} to call. I am not aware that {D.he} called our number before the clamp was cut.\""), .cross("You did not see the defendant cut the clamp, did you?", "\"Not in person. I saw it on the lot camera the next morning. The footage is clear, and I did not need to see it live.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut off a clamp and drove away.", "A driver wronged by a clamp."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid decision and someone else paid for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was told to pay a $100 fee.", "{DL} left the cutters in the trunk."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the clamp off your car?", "\"Yes. I did. I was angry and I used bolt cutters I keep in my trunk. I should not have, and I know that now.\""), .direct("Why did you park in that lot?", "\"I was meeting a friend in the area and could not find street parking. The lot looked open and I saw no sign that said it was private.\""), .direct("What did you think when you saw the clamp?", "\"I was furious. I had been in the lot for twenty minutes, and the notice asked for $100 to release the car. It felt like a trap.\""), .direct("Did you call the number on the notice?", "\"I thought about it. I was late for an appointment and did not want to wait for a technician. I made a decision that I regret.\""), .direct("What do you remember about signs at the lot?", "\"I did not see any when I parked. There may have been one by the entrance, but I came in from the side street.\""), .direct("What would you do differently?", "\"I would have called and paid the fee, then complained to the owner or filed a report afterward. Cutting the clamp made things worse.\""), .cross("You were told to pay a $100 fee to get the car released, weren't you?", "\"Yes. That was written on the notice. I thought it was too much for twenty minutes.\""), .cross("You brought bolt cutters to the car, didn't you?", "\"I keep a pair in my trunk for work. I walked to my car, took them out, and cut the clamp. I should not have done it.\""), .cross("The clamp was destroyed when you cut it, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was cut through. I did not think about the cost to the company.\""), .cross("You drove off without speaking to anyone, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did. I was upset and in a hurry, and I left. I did not leave a note or a number.\""), .cross("You could have called the sheriff's office or the lot owner, couldn't you?", "\"I could have. I did not, and I understand that would have been the right way to handle it.\"")],
        openings: ("A towing company clamped a wheel on {D}'s car for parking in a private lot. {D} came back with bolt cutters, cut the clamp, and drove away. The clamp, worth $450, was ruined.", "{D} parked in a lot with no clear signs and found a clamp and a $100 fee. {D} acted in anger, but the lot was a trap."),
        closings: ("The video shows {D} cutting the clamp, the clamp is in pieces, and the notice told {D} how to get it removed. {D} chose to destroy it.", "{D} did not see a sign and was hit with a clamp and a $100 demand. A driver who loses patience is not a criminal."),
        timeline: [(0, "The clamp is placed."), (0, "Two hours later it is cut."), (1, "The owner finds it."), (2, "Video is pulled.")],
        identified: "A lot camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let barBrokenBottleV1 = SmallCases.make(
