        identified: "A bar camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["selfDefense"])

    static let giftCardDrainV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.giftCardDrain",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Register Three's Voided Gift Card Loads Led Straight to One Cashier", "Online Orders Shipped Near Employee's Home"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Embezzled $11,300 belonging to {D.his} employer by loading gift cards and voiding the cash tendered, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...34,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Over four months, one register recorded dozens of gift card loads that were voided right after activation. The cards were then spent online and shipped to an address near {D}'s home. {DL} says customers asked for refunds and {D.he} followed the store's steps.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Register Journal", "Forty-six loads voided after activation."), E(.digital, 3, "Order Records", "Shipments to an address near {D}'s."), E(.document, 2, "Schedule", "{D} on shift each time.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Refunds", "{DL} says customers asked for refunds.")],
        role: "Asset protection investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did the register journal show over four months?", "\"Forty-six gift card loads at one register that were voided right after activation. The loads were reversed, but the cards had already been activated and could be used.\""), .direct("What happened to the cards after they were voided?", "\"They were spent online. The balances were used within hours, and the orders were shipped to an address near {D}'s home.\""), .direct("How did {D} connect to those loads?", "\"{DL} was the cashier on duty for every one of the forty-six. The schedule shows {DL} on the register each time, and no other cashier had the pattern.\""), .direct("How does a normal gift card sale work at the register?", "\"The cashier scans the card, takes payment, and activates it. A void is only expected if the customer changes their mind before payment, not after activation.\""), .direct("What are the store's rules for voiding an activated card?", "\"A manager has to approve it in the system. None of these forty-six voids has a manager's approval on file.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the shipping address?", "\"The orders were all sent to a relative's address near {D.his} home. The relative's name appears on several of the delivery confirmations.\""), .cross("Customers do sometimes ask for refunds, don't they?", "\"Yes. It happens now and then. Most such requests come before the card is activated, not after.\""), .cross("The store was busy on many of those shifts, wasn't it?", "\"Some shifts were busy. A manager may have been unavailable at times, which is a control weakness.\""), .cross("You cannot say who spent the cards online, can you?", "\"Not from the register journal. The order records link the orders to an address near {DL}'s, but I cannot say who typed the numbers.\""), .cross("The address belongs to a relative, not to the defendant, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. It belongs to a relative of {DL}. It is near {DL}'s home, but it is not {DL}'s own address.\""), .cross("{D} did not hide the voids in the system, did {D.he}?", "\"No. They are in the journal for anyone to see. I would not say {D.he} tried to conceal the voids.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} loaded and voided cards for profit.", "A cashier following refund steps."),
        allocution: "\"I should have told the truth the first time.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} never had a manager approve a void.", "The shipments went to a relative's address."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you void the gift card loads?", "\"Yes. Customers asked for refunds after they had been activated, and I followed the steps I was taught on the register.\""), .direct("Why did you not get a manager to approve the voids?", "\"They were busy and I did not want to interrupt. I thought a void was something I could do myself if the system let me.\""), .direct("What did customers say when they asked for refunds?", "\"Most said they bought the wrong amount or the wrong card. I thought it was best to give the money back and keep them happy.\""), .direct("Did you know the cards were being spent online?", "\"No. I had no idea. I did not know where the cards went after the voids, and I never saw any of the orders.\""), .direct("Why were the shipments sent to a relative's address?", "\"I do not know. I have no knowledge of those orders. A relative lives near me, but I did not ask anyone to ship anything there.\""), .direct("How do you feel about being accused?", "\"I am upset and confused. I did what I thought was right, and I did not take anything from the store.\""), .cross("You were on shift for every one of the forty-six voids, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I work at that register most days. I did not think it meant anything that it was me.\""), .cross("No manager ever approved a void, did one?", "\"No. I did not ask them to. I know the rule now, and I should have followed it.\""), .cross("Customers rarely ask for refunds on activated cards, don't they?", "\"It was not common. I did not think about the number. I just handled each as it came.\""), .cross("The shipments went to a relative's address, didn't they?", "\"I understand that. It is a coincidence, and I do not know how it happened.\""), .cross("You never reported the odd refund requests to anyone, did you?", "\"No. I did not think they were odd. I should have asked a manager, and I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("Over four months, one register recorded forty-six gift card loads that were voided right after activation. The cards were spent online and shipped near {D}'s home.", "{D} followed the store's refund steps for customers who asked. A cashier who processes refunds is not a thief, and the shipments are a coincidence."),
        closings: ("Forty-six voids, no manager approvals, {D} on shift each time, and shipments to a relative's address near {D}'s home. This was no accident.", "{D} processed refunds the way customers asked and the register allowed. Missing manager approvals are a store failing and a training gap, not proof that {D} stole from the store."),
        timeline: [(-120, "The first void."), (-30, "The audit begins."), (0, "The orders are traced."), (5, "{D} is interviewed.")],
        identified: "A register journal.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let rideshareRunnerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.rideshareRunner",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Dash Camera Records Fare Skipping Into a Dark Front Yard", "Rideshare Driver Waits Twenty Minutes Before Calling Deputies"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole $38 in transportation services from {V}, a rideshare driver, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} drove {D} across town in the early morning of {DATE}. At the destination, {D} said {D.he} would get cash and went inside a house and never came back. The fare was $38. {V}'s dash camera captured the whole ride. {DL} says the app declined the card and {D.he} meant to pay.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Dash Camera", "{D} walks away from the car."), E(.digital, 3, "App Record", "The card payment was declined."), E(.document, 1, "Fare Receipt", "$38.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Meant to Pay", "{DL} says {D.he} went to get cash.")],
        role: "Rideshare driver",
        exam: [.direct("Where did you pick up {D} on the morning of {DATE}?", "\"At a pickup point downtown in the early hours. {D} got into the back seat and gave me a destination across town on the other side of the river.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say when you arrived?", "\"That {D.he} would run inside to get cash for the fare. {D.He} got out and walked toward a house, and I waited with the engine running.\""), .direct("What was the fare for the ride?", "\"$38. It was a straight trip across town of about twenty-five minutes, and the app showed the fare when I started.\""), .direct("How long did you wait for the defendant to come back?", "\"About twenty minutes. I watched the door and called the number in the app. The phone went straight to voicemail, so I contacted the app's support.\""), .direct("What does your dash camera show?", "\"The entire ride, with sound. It shows {DL} talking about getting cash, then walking up to the door and going inside without looking back.\""), .direct("What happened with the card on the app?", "\"The payment was declined. The app notified me right after the ride, and the support team confirmed the card on file had failed.\""), .cross("The card was declined, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The app showed a decline for insufficient funds. That is common, and I understand it can happen to anyone.\""), .cross("You called the defendant only after twenty minutes, didn't you?", "\"I waited as long as I could, hoping {DL} would come out. I called and left a message when {DL} did not.\""), .cross("{D} got out of the car without any argument, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. It was calm. {D.He} said {D.he} was getting cash, and I believed it for a while.\""), .cross("You do not know whether the defendant lives at that house, do you?", "\"No. I only know {D.he} walked up to it and went in. I never learned who lives there.\""), .cross("The fare is a small amount, isn't it?", "\"It is $38. It is not a lot, but it is my income, and it matters to me.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} rode and ran from the fare.", "A rider whose card failed."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid decision and someone else paid for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} gave a false door to knock on.", "{DL} turned off the phone."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you run from the fare?", "\"No. I went inside to get cash, and I meant to come back out and pay. I did not plan to skip the fare.\""), .direct("Why did you not come back out?", "\"I sat down inside and fell asleep. I had been out late and I was exhausted. I woke up hours later and the car was gone.\""), .direct("Whose house did you go into?", "\"It was a friend's place. I did not give the driver the right door at first, and I should have been clearer.\""), .direct("Why did the app decline your card?", "\"I did not have enough on the card. I knew it was low, but I thought I had enough for a short ride, and I was wrong.\""), .direct("Why was your phone off?", "\"The battery died. I was out most of the night and did not charge it. That is why the driver could not reach me.\""), .direct("What would you say to the driver?", "\"That I am sorry. I should have paid or at least told the driver what was going on, and I would like to make it right.\""), .cross("You told the driver you would get cash and never came back, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. It looks like I ran, and I understand that. I just fell asleep.\""), .cross("You pointed to a door that was not your own, didn't you?", "\"I pointed to a friend's door. I should have said it was not mine.\""), .cross("Your phone was off when the driver called, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was dead. I did not think about the driver's calls until later.\""), .cross("You knew your card might not work, didn't you?", "\"I thought it might be low. I figured I could get cash if it failed, and that is why I went inside.\""), .cross("You did not contact the driver the next day, did you?", "\"No. I was embarrassed and did not know how. That was my failure.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} drove {D} across town in the early morning. At the destination, {D} said {D.he} would get cash for the $38 fare, walked into a house, and never came back. The dash camera caught it all.", "{D}'s card was declined and {D} went inside for cash. {D} fell asleep and never meant to skip the fare. That is a lapse, not a crime."),
        closings: ("The dash camera, the declined card, and the unanswered calls. {D} said {D.he} would come back and did not, and the phone was off.", "{D} went to get cash, fell asleep, and woke up too late. {D} had no plan to run and is sorry for the trouble."),
        timeline: [(0, "12:40 a.m.: the pickup."), (0, "1:05 a.m.: the drop-off."), (0, "1:25 a.m.: the call."), (1, "The footage is pulled.")],
        identified: "A dash camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let rentalBatAssaultV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.rentalBatAssault",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Skull Fracture After Rent Dispute at Apartment Door; Neighbor's Phone Caught Part", "Owner Says a Knock Preceded the Visit; Tenant Says the Door Was Opened Unannounced"],
        law: "awdwisi",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Assaulted {V} with a deadly weapon, a baseball bat, inflicting serious injury, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A rent dispute at an apartment turned violent on {DATE}. {D} swung a baseball bat and hit {V}, the property owner, causing a skull fracture. A neighbor's phone recorded the last seconds. {DL} says {V} had stepped inside without notice.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Neighbor Video", "{D} swings the bat."), E(.forensic, 3, "Medical Report", "Skull fracture."), E(.physical, 2, "Bat", "Recovered in the apartment.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Unannounced Entry", "{DL} says {V} stepped inside without notice.")],
        role: "Tenant",
        exam: [.direct("How did you come to record the incident on your phone?", "\"I live in the next unit and heard shouting at {D}'s door. I stepped outside and started recording when I saw the owner on the porch and {DL} in the doorway.\""), .direct("What does your video show?", "\"It shows {DL} stepping out with a baseball bat and swinging it at {V}. The last few seconds show {V} falling back against the railing and collapsing.\""), .direct("Where was {V} standing when the bat swung?", "\"On the porch, at the edge of the doorway. {V} was not inside the apartment when I recorded, though I cannot say what happened a moment earlier.\""), .direct("What was the argument about?", "\"Rent. I had heard the owner and {DL} discuss late payments more than once. This time the voices were louder, and I heard {DL} shout to get out.\""), .direct("What happened to {V} after the swing?", "\"{V} fell and did not get up. I called 911 and stayed with {V} until the paramedics arrived. {V} was bleeding from the head.\""), .direct("What did {D} do after the swing?", "\"{D.He} stood in the doorway with the bat for a moment and then dropped it. {D.He} looked shocked and said nothing to me.\""), .cross("{V} stepped toward the doorway before the swing, didn't {V}?", "\"I believe so. {V} was at the door, and I cannot say whether a foot was inside. The video does not show the threshold clearly.\""), .cross("You did not hear whether {V} gave notice before coming, did you?", "\"No. I only know the argument was loud. I do not know whether notice was given, and I do not know what was said before I came outside.\""), .cross("{D} dropped the bat right away, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Within a few seconds. {D.He} did not swing again and did not leave. {D.He} stayed until the deputies came.\""), .cross("The two had argued before, hadn't they?", "\"Yes, about rent and late payments. It was often tense, but I never saw it get physical until that day.\""), .cross("The video does not show the first words spoken, does it?", "\"No. It starts after the voices were already raised. I do not have what was said in the first minute.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} struck {V} with a bat over rent.", "A tenant protecting a home."),
        allocution: "\"I lost my temper, and I'm sorry for what I did.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was two months behind.", "{V} was on the porch when struck."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you swing the bat and hit {V}?", "\"Yes. I did. I have replayed it over and over, and I wish more than anything I could take it back.\""), .direct("Why did you pick up the bat?", "\"I was scared. {V} had stepped inside without any notice, and I did not know what {V} wanted. I grabbed the bat next to the door.\""), .direct("How far was {V} into your apartment when you swung?", "\"At the door, with one foot over the threshold. I felt like {V} was coming at me, and I swung before I thought about it.\""), .direct("What was your financial situation at the time?", "\"I was two months behind on rent because I lost hours at work. I had been trying to work something out with {V}.\""), .direct("What did you do after you hit {V}?", "\"I dropped the bat and called for help. I felt sick. I stood there until the neighbor called, and I stayed until deputies arrived.\""), .direct("What would you say to {V}?", "\"That I am sorry. I did not mean to hurt {V} like that, and I think about it every day.\""), .cross("{V} was on the porch when you swung, wasn't {V}?", "\"At the door, on the porch side. I understand the video shows that. I felt {V} was inside, and I was frightened.\""), .cross("You were two months behind on rent, weren't you?", "\"Yes. It was a hardship, and I was working on it. I was stressed and exhausted, and I know that is not an excuse.\""), .cross("You grabbed a bat and swung at someone's head, didn't you?", "\"I did. It was a terrible choice, and I know I could have shut the door or called the sheriff's office.\""), .cross("{V} did not have a weapon, did {V}?", "\"No. I did not see one, and I know that now. I was afraid, and I misjudged what was happening.\""), .cross("You could have closed the door, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have. I did not think. I reacted, and a person was badly hurt.\"")],
        openings: ("A rent dispute turned violent when {D} swung a baseball bat and hit {V}, the property owner, causing a skull fracture. A neighbor recorded the last seconds on a phone.", "{D} was two months behind and frightened when {V} stepped inside without notice. {D} reacted in fear, and that is not the same as meaning to hurt someone."),
        closings: ("The video shows {D} swinging a bat at someone standing on the porch. {V} has a fractured skull, and {D} chose to swing.", "{V} came to the door without notice and {D} was afraid. Fear and a bad choice made in seconds are not the same as intent to injure."),
        timeline: [(-60, "Rent falls behind."), (-1, "A notice."), (0, "The blow."), (1, "Surgery.")],
        identified: "A neighbor's video.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["selfDefense"])

    static let consignmentShopV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.consignmentShop",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Shop's Closing Leaves Two Dozen Sellers Unpaid; Fur Coat Was Sold Months Earlier", "Owner Spent Sale Proceeds on Rent and Loans"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 9,
        spec: "Having been entrusted as consignee with property belonging to {V}, sold it and fraudulently converted the proceeds, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 34...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} ran a consignment shop for six years. When it closed on {DATE}, twenty-three sellers were owed $11,300. {V} had left a dining set and a fur coat, both sold months earlier without payment. {DL} says sales were slow and the shop was going under.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Sales Records", "The dining set and the coat were sold."), E(.document, 3, "Payout Ledger", "23 sellers unpaid, $11,300."), E(.document, 3, "Bank Statements", "Proceeds used for rent and loans.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Slow Sales", "{DL} says business collapsed.")],
        role: "Consignor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you leave at the consignment shop?", "\"A dining set and a fur coat. I signed a consignment agreement and the shop agreed to pay me a share of the price once each item sold.\""), .direct("What did the sales records show about my items?", "\"Both items sold, the dining set about five months before the shop closed and the coat a month after. The records list the sale prices and the dates.\""), .direct("Was I paid anything from those sales?", "\"No. I called and went by the shop several times. I was told checks were coming, and none ever came before the shop closed.\""), .direct("How many other sellers were owed money?", "\"Twenty-three in all, with a total of $11,300. I learned that when we all received the same notice after the shop shut down.\""), .direct("What did the shop's bank statements show about the proceeds?", "\"That sale money went toward rent and loan payments. The deposits from sales did not go into a separate account for sellers.\""), .direct("How did {D} respond when you asked for payment?", "\"{D} apologized each time and said money was tight. {D.He} asked me to be patient and said checks would go out soon.\""), .cross("Sales at the shop fell during the last year, didn't they?", "\"I understand they did. That is what {D.he} told me. I did not see the shop's books, and I cannot say how much.\""), .cross("The consignment agreement gave the defendant time to pay, didn't it?", "\"It said payment within thirty days after sale. {D.He} was months late on mine. I do not recall any extension.\""), .cross("{D} offered to return unsold items to other sellers, didn't {D.he}?", "\"I heard that. My items were sold, so that did not apply to me.\""), .cross("The shop was open for six years without trouble, wasn't it?", "\"Yes, I used it before. It was fine until this year. I would not have left my coat there if I had known.\""), .cross("You do not know whether the defendant planned to pay when the items sold, do you?", "\"No. I can only say that I was not paid. I do not know what was in {D.his} mind.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold consigned goods and kept the money.", "A shop failing."),
        allocution: "\"I should have told the truth the first time.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept taking new goods after the first unpaid check.", "{DL} used the money for rent."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you sell {V}'s dining set and coat and keep the money?", "\"I sold them and used the money to keep the shop open. I intended to pay {V} when I could, and I know I did not.\""), .direct("Why did you use the money for rent and loans?", "\"Sales were slow and I was behind. I thought if I could get through a few more months, I could catch up and pay everyone.\""), .direct("Why did you keep taking new goods after you missed the first payment?", "\"I needed stock to keep customers coming. I thought new items would sell and fix the problem. That was a mistake.\""), .direct("What did you tell sellers who asked about payment?", "\"That checks would go out soon. I meant it. I kept hoping the next month would be better, and it was not.\""), .direct("How did the shop close?", "\"The landlord locked the door after I fell behind on rent. I lost the shop and the stock. I felt like I had failed everyone.\""), .direct("What do you want the sellers to know?", "\"That I am sorry. I did not mean to take anyone's money. I want to find a way to repay each of them.\""), .cross("You used sellers' money for your own rent, didn't you?", "\"The shop's rent. I understand it was not mine to use. I should have kept it separate.\""), .cross("You kept accepting new goods after you stopped paying, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have stopped. I told myself it would work out, and it did not.\""), .cross("You told {V} that a check was coming, and it never came, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said it more than once. I meant it each time, and I did not follow through.\""), .cross("Twenty-three sellers are owed $11,300, aren't they?", "\"Yes. That is the total. I know I owe each of them, and I mean to pay.\""), .cross("You never set aside sale proceeds for sellers, did you?", "\"No. I put everything in one account. I should have had a separate one, and I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("When {D}'s consignment shop closed, twenty-three sellers were owed $11,300. {V} had left a dining set and a fur coat that were both sold months earlier without payment.", "{D} ran a shop that fell on hard times and used sale money to keep it open. {D} meant to pay everyone, and the shop failed first."),
        closings: ("Items sold, money spent on rent and loans, twenty-three sellers unpaid, and new goods accepted after the first missed check. {D} took sellers' property and kept the proceeds.", "{D} ran the shop for six years and it collapsed. {D} meant to repay every seller, and a failing business is not the same as a theft."),
        timeline: [(-240, "The coat is sold."), (-90, "The first unpaid check."), (0, "The shop closes."), (14, "Sellers complain.")],
        identified: "A sales ledger.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let cameraSmashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.cameraSmash",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Neighbor Pulls Driveway Camera Off Pole With Pry Bar, Cracks Lens; Second Camera Records It", "Dispute Over Camera That Faced a Driveway"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a driveway security camera, causing damage of $230, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...66,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} mounted a security camera on a pole after a series of break-ins on the street. On {DATE}, {D}, a neighbor, pulled it off the pole with a pry bar and cracked the lens. A second camera across the street recorded {D} doing it. The camera cost $230 to replace. {DL} says the camera faced {D.his} driveway and {D.his} children.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Second Camera", "{D} pulls the camera down with a pry bar."), E(.document, 2, "Receipt", "$230 for the camera."), E(.physical, 1, "Cracked Lens", "A lens with a pry mark.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Faced Driveway", "{DL} says the lens faced {D.his} driveway."), E(.statement, 1, "Children", "{DL} says {D.his} children play there.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What did the camera across the street record?", "\"It shows {D} walking up to the pole, putting a pry bar behind the camera, and pulling it down. The camera fell to the ground and the lens cracked.\""), .direct("What tool did {D} use?", "\"A pry bar, about two feet long. It was recovered from {D.his} garage and had paint transfer that matched the pole.\""), .direct("What was the damage to the camera?", "\"A cracked lens and a pry mark on the housing. The camera cost $230 to replace, and the receipt is in evidence.\""), .direct("Why did {V} install the camera?", "\"There had been several break-ins on the street, including a car and a shed. {V} installed it to watch the street and the sidewalks.\""), .direct("What did you find when you checked the camera's field of view?", "\"It covered the street and the sidewalk. It did not look into {D.his} yard or windows. I checked the recorded angle against the property lines.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say when you spoke to {D.him}?", "\"{D.He} said the camera faced {D.his} driveway and the area where {D.his} children play. {D.he} said {D.he} was protecting them.\""), .cross("{D} sent a text before this, didn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. {D.He} texted that {D.he} would take the camera down. That text is in the evidence.\""), .cross("The camera was close to the defendant's property line, wasn't it?", "\"It was on a pole at the edge of the street. It was not far from {D.his} driveway, but the view still pointed at the street.\""), .cross("{D} did not hide what {D.he} was doing, did {D.he}?", "\"No. It was done in daylight, in plain view of the camera across the street.\""), .cross("{D} has young children, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. They play in the front yard. A parent may worry about a camera nearby.\""), .cross("No one asked {V} to move the camera before it came down, did they?", "\"Not that I know of. There was no written request, and I did not find any conversation about it.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} tore down a neighbor's camera.", "A parent protecting children."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had threatened to 'take it down' in a text.", "The camera's field of view covered the street, not {DL}'s home."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you pull the camera down?", "\"Yes. I did, with a pry bar. I was angry, and I thought I was protecting my kids.\""), .direct("Why did you believe the camera faced your driveway?", "\"From where I stood, the lens seemed to point toward my house. My kids play out front, and I did not like a camera watching them.\""), .direct("Did you ask {V} to move the camera?", "\"No. I should have. I got upset and decided to handle it myself, and that was a mistake.\""), .direct("What did you mean by the text that said you would take it down?", "\"I was venting. I did not think I would actually do it, and I did not think about how it would be seen.\""), .direct("What did you do after you pulled it down?", "\"I put it on {V}'s porch. I left a note saying I was sorry. I felt bad as soon as I did it.\""), .direct("How do you feel about it now?", "\"I feel foolish. I should have talked to {V} or asked the sheriff's office to look at the angle. I will pay for the camera.\""), .cross("You texted that you would take it down before you did, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was upset. I did not think I would follow through, and then I did.\""), .cross("The camera faced the street, not your driveway, didn't it?", "\"The deputy says so. I thought otherwise at the time. I should have checked before I acted.\""), .cross("You did not ask {V} first, did you?", "\"No. I should have. I let my anger make the decision.\""), .cross("You used a pry bar and cracked the lens, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not mean to crack it, but I did not take care either.\""), .cross("You could have called the sheriff's office about the camera, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I could have. I did not, and I understand that was the better way.\"")],
        openings: ("After a string of break-ins, {V} mounted a camera on a pole. {D} pulled it down with a pry bar and cracked the lens, and a second camera recorded it. The camera cost $230.", "{D} believed a neighbor's camera was watching {D.his} driveway and {D.his} children. {D} acted rashly, but out of concern as a parent."),
